@H1:RECITALS
@P:**A. The Loan.** Lender has agreed to make a loan to Borrower in the original principal amount of Fourteen Million Seven Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($14,750,000.00) (the "**Loan**"), on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in that certain Term Sheet — Commercial Real Estate Loan, dated April 1, 2025, bearing Deal Reference CHB CRE Loan No. 2025-CHS-0047, executed by Lender, Borrower, and Guarantor (the "**Term Sheet**"), and in the other Loan Documents. The Loan will be evidenced by a promissory note in the original principal amount of the Loan (the "**Note**") and will be advanced in two components: an initial advance of Twelve Million Five Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($12,500,000.00) at closing (the "**Initial Advance**"), and a renovation holdback of Two Million Two Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($2,250,000.00) (the "**Renovation Holdback**"), to be disbursed on a draw basis in accordance with Article 10.
@P:**B. Purpose.** The proceeds of the Loan are being applied toward (i) the acquisition by Borrower of the Property, (ii) costs of the renovation of the improvements located on the Property, and (iii) closing costs, reserves, and other costs approved by Lender. The purchase price of the Property is Seventeen Million Eight Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($17,800,000.00), and the total budgeted cost of the renovation is Three Million One Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($3,150,000.00).
@P:**C. Guaranties and Environmental Indemnity.** The Loan is structured as non-recourse to Borrower except as expressly provided in Article 17. The obligations of Borrower are supported by (i) a Guaranty Agreement dated as of the Closing Date executed by Neil Ashford Graydon, an individual residing at 14 Church Street, Charleston, South Carolina 29401 ("**Guarantor**"), comprising the non-recourse carve-out guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, and the payment guaranty for interest shortfall described in the Term Sheet (the "**Guaranty**"), and (ii) an Environmental Indemnity Agreement dated as of the Closing Date executed by Borrower and Guarantor (the "**Environmental Indemnity**").
@P:**D. Security.** As a condition to making the Loan, Lender requires that it be granted a valid, enforceable, first-priority lien on and security interest in the Property, that it be granted a present and absolute assignment of all Leases and Rents, and that it be granted a security interest in all personal property, fixtures, accounts, contracts, permits, and other collateral described below.
@P:**E. Environmental Matter.** Lender has received that certain Phase I Environmental Site Assessment prepared by Clearfield Environmental Consulting LLC, Report No. CLR-2025-0119, dated January 28, 2025 (the "**Phase I ESA**"), which identifies one Controlled Recognized Environmental Condition on Lot 7 of the Property, addressed by the South Carolina Department of Health and Environmental Control ("**SCDHEC**") No Further Action letter dated August 12, 2021 for SCDHEC Site ID No. SC-29403-0772, and subject to the recorded Land Use Restriction described in Article 9.
@P:NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the foregoing recitals and of the Loan and the covenants and agreements set forth herein, and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, Borrower and Lender agree as follows:

@H1:ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION
@H2:1.1|Defined Terms.|As used in this Mortgage, the following terms have the following meanings. Terms defined elsewhere in this Mortgage have the meanings there ascribed to them.
@I:"**Advance**" means any disbursement of the proceeds of the Loan made by Lender, whether the Initial Advance, any disbursement of the Renovation Holdback, or any protective advance made under Section 16.10.
@I:"**Affiliate**" means, with respect to any Person, any other Person that directly or indirectly Controls, is Controlled by, or is under common Control with, such Person. "Control" means the possession, directly or indirectly, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of a Person, whether through ownership of voting interests, by contract, or otherwise.
@I:"**Applicable Law**" means all federal, state, and local statutes, ordinances, codes, rules, regulations, orders, permits, licenses, judgments, and decrees applicable to Borrower, any Related Entity, the Property, or the Loan, including without limitation the Requirements of Law described in Section 6.5, all Environmental Laws, the applicable requirements of Title XI of the Financial Institutions Reform, Recovery, and Enforcement Act of 1989 ("**FIRREA**"), and the flood insurance requirements of the Flood Disaster Protection Act of 1973 and Regulations thereunder.
@I:"**Architect**" means the architect of record engaged by Borrower for the Renovation Work, licensed to practice in the State of South Carolina and reasonably acceptable to Lender.
@I:"**Business Day**" means any day other than a Saturday, Sunday, or day on which national banks are authorized or required to be closed in the State of Georgia or the State of South Carolina.
@I:"**Capital Replacement Reserve**" means the reserve account established and funded pursuant to Section 11.2.
@I:"**Completion Guaranty**" means the completion guaranty component of the Guaranty, pursuant to which Guarantor unconditionally guarantees the completion of the Renovation Work in accordance with the Plans, within the Renovation Budget, and on or before the Substantial Completion Deadline, without any cap based upon the amount of the Renovation Budget or the Renovation Holdback.
@I:"**Construction Contract**" means that certain executed construction contract between Borrower, as owner, and Beaufort Builders Group LLC, South Carolina General Contractor License No. SC-GC-47921, as general contractor, in the contract sum of Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($2,850,000.00), covering hard costs of construction, together with all schedules, exhibits, amendments, change orders, and supplements thereto, and all warranties, guaranties, and indemnities relating thereto.
@I:"**Debt**" means the aggregate of all obligations and liabilities of Borrower to Lender under the Note, this Mortgage, and the other Loan Documents, whether now existing or hereafter arising, direct or indirect, absolute or contingent, including without limitation all principal, interest (including interest at the Default Rate), the Yield Maintenance Premium, late charges, prepayment premiums, escrow and reserve deficiencies, protective advances, costs of collection, reasonable attorneys' fees, and all other sums advanced by Lender on behalf of Borrower, together with interest on all such sums at the Default Rate.
@I:"**Default Rate**" means the Note Rate plus five percent (5.00%) per annum, as more particularly provided in Section 3.4.
@I:"**DSCR**" has the meaning given in Section 14.1.
@I:"**Environmental Indemnity**" has the meaning given in Recital C.
@I:"**Environmental Laws**" means all federal, state, and local statutes, regulations, ordinances, and orders relating to pollution, protection of the environment, human health, or Hazardous Substances, including without limitation the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation, and Liability Act, 42 U.S.C. § 9601 et seq. ("**CERCLA**"), the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act, 42 U.S.C. § 6901 et seq., the Clean Water Act, the Clean Air Act, the Toxic Substances Control Act, and the South Carolina Pollution Control Act and the South Carolina Hazardous Waste Management Act, together with all regulations, guidance, and institutional controls promulgated or imposed thereunder.
@I:"**Escrow Funds**" means all funds deposited with or held by Lender pursuant to Article 11, together with all interest and earnings thereon (if any).
@I:"**Event of Default**" means any event or condition described in Section 15.1.
@I:"**GAAP**" means generally accepted accounting principles in the United States, consistently applied.
@I:"**Governmental Authority**" means the United States, the State of South Carolina, the City of Charleston, the County of Charleston, SCDHEC, and any other federal, state, regional, or local body or agency having jurisdiction over Borrower, any Related Entity, the Property, or any part thereof.
@I:"**Hazardous Substances**" means any substance, material, or waste that is regulated, listed, defined, or classified as hazardous, toxic, a pollutant, a contaminant, or a hazardous waste under any Environmental Law, including without limitation petroleum and petroleum products, perchloroethylene and other volatile organic compounds, polychlorinated biphenyls, asbestos-containing materials, lead-based paint, and radioactive materials.
@I:"**Impositions**" means all real estate taxes, assessments, water and sewer charges, license fees, permit fees, and other governmental charges levied against the Property, and all insurance premiums required under Article 12.
@I:"**Improvements**" means all buildings, structures, and improvements now or hereafter located on the Land, including without limitation the mixed-use building containing three ground-floor retail bays (Bays 1, 2, and 3) and two upper-floor office suites (Suites A and B) containing approximately 31,000 square feet of gross building area, together with all fixtures and building systems, including all HVAC equipment, the passenger elevator, plumbing, electrical systems, fire protection and fire suppression systems, and the decorative iron balcony on the King Street elevation.
@I:"**Independent Manager**" means a natural person who (a) is not, and has never been, a member, manager, officer, employee, creditor, or Affiliate of Borrower, Guarantor, any Related Entity, or any of their respective Affiliates; (b) has no economic interest in Borrower, Guarantor, or any Related Entity; (c) is not a party to any agreement with Borrower, Guarantor, or any Related Entity that would impair such person's independent judgment; and (d) is provided by a nationally recognized independent director service or is otherwise approved in writing by Lender.
@I:"**Initial Advance**" has the meaning given in Recital A.
@I:"**Land**" means the real property described on **Exhibit A**, comprising Lots 7, 8, and 9 of the Hampstead Village Plat (Charleston County Tax Map Nos. 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009) and that certain strip of land formerly known as Anson Lane vacated by City of Charleston Ordinance No. 2019-084 and conveyed by quitclaim deed recorded in the RMC Office at Deed Book 1128, Page 443.
@I:"**Leases**" means each and every lease, sublease, license, occupancy agreement, and other agreement (including any guaranty of any thereof) now or hereafter affecting the Property or any part thereof, together with all amendments, extensions, renewals, and modifications thereof, including without limitation the three Leases identified on the certified rent roll delivered to Lender at closing (the "**Rent Roll**"), namely the Lowcountry Provisions Inc. Lease, the Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC Lease, and the Tidemark Consulting Group LLC Lease.
@I:"**Loan Documents**" means, collectively, the Note, this Mortgage, the Guaranty, the Environmental Indemnity, the UCC-1 financing statement and any fixture filing, each reserve or escrow agreement (if any) executed in connection with the Loan, each estoppel certificate, subordination, non-disturbance, and attornment agreement, and each other document, instrument, or certificate now or hereafter executed by Borrower, Guarantor, or any other Person in connection with the Loan, as each may be amended, restated, or supplemented from time to time. The Construction Contract and the Renovation Budget are not Loan Documents; they are Project Documents assigned to Lender as additional collateral pursuant to Section 2.2.
@I:"**LUR**" means that certain Land Use Restriction and institutional control recorded in the RMC Office at Deed Book 1203, Page 89, imposed by SCDHEC in connection with SCDHEC Site ID No. SC-29403-0772, as more particularly described in Article 9.
@I:"**Maturity Date**" means April 15, 2030.
@I:"**NFA Letter**" means the SCDHEC "No Further Action" letter dated August 12, 2021 issued with respect to SCDHEC Site ID No. SC-29403-0772, together with all conditions, attachments, and institutional controls referenced therein.
@I:"**Note**" and "**Note Rate**" have the meanings given in Recital A and Section 3.1, respectively.
@I:"**OFAC**" means the Office of Foreign Assets Control of the United States Department of the Treasury.
@I:"**Operating Agreement**" means the Amended and Restated Operating Agreement of Borrower, effective as of January 12, 2024, as amended through March 1, 2025, and as further amended by the Operating Agreement Amendment described in Section 7.6.
@I:"**Permits**" means all permits, licenses, approvals, entitlements, development rights, variances, special exceptions, certificates of occupancy, sign permits, encroachment licenses, and other governmental authorizations relating to the Property or the Renovation Work, including without limitation all approvals of the City of Charleston Board of Architectural Review ("**BAR**").
@I:"**Permitted Exceptions**" means those matters listed on **Exhibit B** and approved by Lender in writing, and no others.
@I:"**Person**" means any individual, corporation, limited liability company, partnership, trust, joint venture, unincorporated association, Governmental Authority, or other entity.
@I:"**Personal Property**" means all of the following, wherever located, whether now owned or hereafter acquired: all equipment, machinery, fixtures and building systems (including goods that are or are to become fixtures), furniture, furnishings, trade fixtures, inventory, goods, supplies, materials, accounts, deposit accounts, chattel paper, instruments, documents, letters of credit and letter-of-credit rights, supporting obligations, investment property, commercial tort claims, general intangibles, payment intangibles, software and computer records, together with all Permits, Plans, warranties, guaranties, indemnities, and claims against third parties (including claims under the Construction Contract), all Leases and Rents, all Insurance Proceeds and Condemnation Awards, all Escrow Funds and Reserve Accounts, all books and records relating to any of the foregoing, and all products, accessions, substitutions, replacements, and proceeds of any of the foregoing.
@I:"**Plans**" means the final plans, specifications, and drawings for the Renovation Work approved by Lender and by all required Governmental Authorities, as amended by change orders approved in accordance with Section 10.8.
@I:"**Project Documents**" means the Construction Contract, the Plans, the Renovation Budget, all architectural, engineering, and construction management agreements, all Permits, all warranties and guaranties relating to the Renovation Work, and all other contracts relating to the acquisition, renovation, leasing, operation, or maintenance of the Property.
@I:"**Property**" means, collectively, the Land, the Improvements, the Personal Property, the Leases, the Rents, the Escrow Funds, and all other property, rights, and interests described in Article 2, and every part and parcel thereof.
@I:"**Related Entities**" means Graydon Development Group LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company and the managing member of Borrower ("**GDG**" or the "**Managing Member**"); Tidewater Opportunity Fund II LP, a Delaware limited partnership ("**Tidewater**"); Harborline Capital Advisors LLC, a Delaware limited liability company ("**Harborline**"); and each other Person that directly or indirectly owns any equity interest in Borrower (collectively with GDG, Tidewater, and Harborline, the "**Members**").
@I:"**Rents**" means all rents, issues, profits, revenues, income, receipts, security deposits, advance rents, common area maintenance and operating expense reimbursements, tax and insurance contributions, percentage rent, parking income, concession and license fees, and all other sums now or hereafter payable under or in connection with the Leases or the use or occupancy of the Property, including all sums payable as damages or in settlement of any claim relating thereto.
@I:"**Renovation Budget**" means the budget for the Renovation Work in the total amount of Three Million One Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($3,150,000.00), as summarized on **Exhibit C** and as more particularly described on Schedule 3 to the Term Sheet, as the same may be modified only with Lender's prior written consent.
@I:"**Renovation Holdback**" has the meaning given in Recital A and is more particularly described in Article 10.
@I:"**Renovation Work**" means the renovation, restoration, and improvement of the Improvements contemplated by the Plans and the Renovation Budget, including without limitation the HVAC replacement, elevator modernization, façade restoration, tenant improvement work for vacant space, and related soft costs and contingency described on **Exhibit C**.
@I:"**Reserve Accounts**" means the Tax and Insurance Escrow, the Capital Replacement Reserve, the TI/LC Reserve, and the Renovation Reserve, together with any other reserve or escrow account established in connection with the Loan.
@I:"**SPE**" and "**Single-Purpose Entity**" have the meanings given in Section 7.1.
@I:"**Substantial Completion**" means the completion of all Renovation Work in accordance with the Plans, as certified by the Architect, and the issuance by the City of Charleston of a certificate of occupancy (or equivalent final inspection approval) for the renovated portions of the Property, subject only to punch-list items and retainage acceptable to Lender.
@I:"**Substantial Completion Deadline**" means June 15, 2026, being the date fourteen (14) months after the Closing Date.
@I:"**Survey**" means the current ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey of the Land prepared by Cartwright Land Surveying LLC, dated January 15, 2025 and recorded in the RMC Office at Plat Book 64, Page 91, conforming to the 2021 Minimum Standard Detail Requirements for ALTA/NSPS Land Title Surveys, certified to Lender, the Title Insurer, and Borrower, and re-certified to a date not more than ninety (90) days prior to the Closing Date.
@I:"**Tenants**" means the tenants, subtenants, licensees, and occupants under the Leases, including without limitation Lowcountry Provisions Inc., Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC, and Tidemark Consulting Group LLC.
@I:"**TI/LC Reserve**" means the tenant improvement and leasing commission reserve established and funded pursuant to Section 11.3.
@I:"**Title Insurer**" means Prestige Title & Settlement Services LLC, as authorized agent for Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc.
@I:"**Title Policy**" means the ALTA Loan Policy (6-17-06) with South Carolina modifications to be issued by the Title Insurer in the amount of $14,750,000.00 pursuant to Commitment No. PT-2025-04-1178 (effective date February 28, 2025), insuring the lien of this Mortgage as a first priority lien, subject only to the Permitted Exceptions, together with all endorsements required by Lender.
@I:"**UCC**" means the Uniform Commercial Code as enacted in the State of South Carolina, S.C. Code Ann. § 36-1-101 et seq.
@I:"**Yield Maintenance Period**" means the period commencing on the date that is twenty-four (24) months after the Closing Date and ending on the date that is forty-eight (48) months after the Closing Date.
@H2:1.2|Rules of Interpretation.|(a) Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation. (b) The words "include," "includes," and "including" are deemed to be followed by "without limitation." (c) References to Articles, Sections, and Exhibits are to Articles and Sections of and Exhibits to this Mortgage. (d) "Hereof," "herein," and "hereunder" refer to this Mortgage as a whole. (e) References to any agreement or instrument are to it as amended, restated, or supplemented in accordance with its terms and, where Lender's consent is required, with Lender's consent. (f) Words in the singular include the plural and vice versa. (g) "Writing" and "written" include electronic transmission. (h) Any reference to a statute or regulation includes any successor provision.
@H2:1.3|Time of the Essence.|Time is of the essence with respect to each obligation of Borrower under this Mortgage, including without limitation the Substantial Completion Deadline and each payment due date.
@H2:1.4|Accounting Terms.|All accounting terms not otherwise defined herein have the meanings assigned to them under GAAP, and all financial computations and determinations shall be made in accordance with GAAP consistently applied.
@H2:1.5|No Construction Against Drafter.|This Mortgage is the product of negotiation between sophisticated parties represented by counsel. It shall not be construed more strictly against either party as the drafter.
@H2:1.6|Relationship to Term Sheet and Other Loan Documents.|This Mortgage and the other Loan Documents implement the Term Sheet. Each provision of the Term Sheet relating to the security for, and the terms of repayment of, the Loan is incorporated herein by reference. To the extent of any conflict between the Term Sheet and this Mortgage, the terms of this Mortgage shall control as between Borrower and Lender, except that no provision of this Mortgage shall be construed to reduce any obligation expressly assumed by Borrower under the Term Sheet unless such reduction is expressly stated herein. In the event of any conflict between this Mortgage and the Note with respect to the determination of the Note Rate, the amount of any payment, or the day-count convention, the Note shall control.
TXTEOF
wc -w $WORKSPACE_DIR/build/mortgage.txt"}

