@H1:ARTICLE 2 — GRANTING CLAUSES AND CREATION OF LIENS
@H2:2.1|Mortgage of Real Property.|For good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, and as security for the prompt, complete, and indefeasible payment and performance of the Debt, Borrower does hereby mortgage, grant, bargain, sell, convey, assign, transfer, pledge, hypothecate, and set over to Lender, its successors and assigns, with mortgage covenants and warranty of title, all of Borrower's right, title, and interest in and to the following (collectively, the "**Mortgaged Property**"):
@I:(a) the Land, being the fee simple estate in and to all those certain lots, pieces, or parcels of land situate, lying, and being in the City of Charleston, County of Charleston, State of South Carolina, known and designated as Lots 7, 8, and 9 of the Hampstead Village Plat, as recorded in Plat Book 41 at Page 218, RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, and designated as Charleston County Tax Map Nos. 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009, as more particularly described on **Exhibit A**;
@I:(b) TOGETHER WITH that certain strip or parcel of land formerly constituting a portion of Anson Lane, a public street vacated and closed by the City of Charleston pursuant to Ordinance No. 2019-084 and conveyed to Borrower's predecessor in title by quitclaim deed recorded in the RMC Office at Deed Book 1128, Page 443, being adjacent to and contiguous with Lot 7 as shown on the Survey and described on **Exhibit A** (the Land described in clauses (a) and (b), collectively, the "**Land**");
@I:(c) TOGETHER WITH the Improvements and all buildings, structures, fixtures, and building systems now or hereafter erected, constructed, placed, or installed on the Land, including without limitation all HVAC equipment and ductwork, the passenger elevator, plumbing, electrical systems, fire protection and fire suppression systems, the roof membrane system, and the decorative iron balcony on the King Street elevation;
@I:(d) TOGETHER WITH all and singular the tenements, hereditaments, easements, rights-of-way, privileges, liberties, appurtenances, and advantages whatsoever to the Land or the Improvements belonging or in any way appertaining, including all development rights, air rights, water, water rights, and riparian rights;
@I:(e) TOGETHER WITH all zoning and land use entitlements, Permits, approvals, and development rights affecting the Property, and all rights of Borrower under any reciprocal easement, access, or operating agreement affecting the Property;
@I:(f) and all estate, right, title, interest, claim, and demand whatsoever, both at law and in equity, of Borrower in and to the Property, together with all reversions, remainders, and rights of redemption arising upon the foreclosure or other enforcement hereof; provided that nothing herein shall constitute a waiver of any right of redemption that cannot lawfully be waived under Applicable Law.
@H2:2.2|Security Interest in Personal Property.|As further security for the Debt, Borrower hereby grants to Lender a continuing security interest under the UCC in all of Borrower's right, title, and interest in and to the Personal Property, including without limitation the following categories of collateral: all equipment, machinery, fixtures (including goods that are or are to become fixtures), furniture, furnishings, trade fixtures, inventory, goods, and supplies; all accounts, deposit accounts, chattel paper, instruments, documents, letter-of-credit rights, investment property, supporting obligations, payment intangibles, general intangibles, commercial tort claims, and software; all Permits, Plans, and Project Documents (including the Construction Contract and all claims, rights of action, and remedies thereunder); all Leases and Rents (as more particularly provided in Article 4); all Insurance Proceeds and Condemnation Awards; all Escrow Funds and Reserve Accounts and all sums now or hereafter deposited therein; all warranties, guaranties, indemnities, and claims against the General Contractor, the Architect, any subcontractor, supplier, tenant, or other Person relating to the Property or the Renovation Work; all books, records, files, and data (in whatever medium) relating to any of the foregoing; and all products, accessions, substitutions, replacements, and proceeds of every kind and description of any of the foregoing. Borrower authorizes Lender to file such UCC financing statements, continuation statements, amendments, and fixture filings as Lender deems necessary or desirable to perfect or maintain the perfection of the security interest granted hereby, including financing statements describing the collateral as "all assets" or "all personal property," and Borrower shall execute and deliver such further instruments as Lender may reasonably request.
@H2:2.3|Fixture Filing.|This Mortgage constitutes a fixture filing under the UCC. For purposes of such filing: (a) the debtor is Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company, whose mailing address is 88 Broad Street, Suite 200, Charleston, South Carolina 29401, South Carolina Secretary of State Filing No. 2024-0011287, federal employer identification number 84-6213750; (b) the secured party is Calverley Heritage Bank, whose mailing address is 412 Whitaker Street, Savannah, Georgia 31401; (c) the collateral includes goods that are or are to become fixtures on the Land, including all HVAC equipment, the elevator and elevator equipment, plumbing, electrical, fire protection, and other building systems, and all other fixtures now or hereafter affixed to the Property; (d) the record owner of the Land is Borrower; (e) the name of the record owner and the debtor is identical; and (f) this Mortgage is to be recorded in the real estate records of Charleston County, South Carolina, in the RMC Office, which is the office authorized under the UCC for the filing of a financing statement covering fixtures with respect to the Land. Borrower shall also execute and deliver a UCC-1 financing statement for filing with the South Carolina Secretary of State naming Borrower as debtor and Lender as secured party and covering all Personal Property, together with a fixture filing for recordation in the RMC Office.
@H2:2.4|Absolute Assignment of Leases and Rents.|Borrower hereby absolutely, presently, and unconditionally grants, transfers, and assigns to Lender all of its right, title, and interest in and to all Leases and Rents, as more particularly provided in Article 4. The assignment effected by this Section 2.4 and by Article 4 is an absolute and present assignment and not a collateral assignment made as additional security only. No separate instrument of assignment of leases and rents shall be required or executed; the assignment of leases and rents required by the Term Sheet and the Title Commitment is incorporated in this Mortgage.
@H2:2.5|Reserved.
@H2:2.6|No Impairment of Title.|Borrower warrants that it has good and marketable fee simple title to the Property, free and clear of all liens, encumbrances, and claims except the Permitted Exceptions, and that Borrower has the right, full power, and lawful authority to mortgage, grant, assign, and pledge the Property as provided herein. Borrower shall, at its sole cost, warrant and defend the title to the Property and the validity and priority of the liens and security interests created hereby against all claims and demands of all Persons.
@H2:2.7|Defeasance; Release.|If Borrower pays and performs the Debt and all other obligations secured hereby when due (or within any applicable grace or cure period), then this Mortgage and the estates, liens, and security interests granted hereby shall be released, satisfied, and discharged of record at Borrower's cost and expense, and Lender shall execute and deliver a satisfaction of mortgage and appropriate UCC termination statements within a commercially reasonable time following written request and payment of Lender's reasonable costs. The release of any part of the Property shall not release or affect the lien of this Mortgage on the remainder.
@H2:2.8|Future Advances; Amount Secured.|This Mortgage secures not only the Initial Advance but also each disbursement of the Renovation Holdback and each protective advance made by Lender. Each disbursement of the Renovation Holdback is an obligatory advance that Lender is obligated to make upon satisfaction of the conditions set forth in Article 10, and the lien of this Mortgage securing each such advance shall have the same priority as the lien securing the Initial Advance, subject to Applicable Law governing the priority of obligatory advances. The maximum principal amount of the Debt secured hereby, exclusive of interest, protective advances, and costs, is $14,750,000.00. Lender is not obligated to make any advance that would cause the outstanding principal balance of the Loan to exceed such amount.
@H2:2.9|No Power of Sale.|Nothing in this Mortgage shall be construed to grant Lender a power of sale or any right to sell the Property without judicial process. The State of South Carolina is a judicial foreclosure jurisdiction, and Lender's remedies upon an Event of Default shall be exercised exclusively through such judicial proceedings and such other remedies as are permitted by Applicable Law.
@H2:2.10|Preservation of Lien After Foreclosure of Prior Encumbrance.|If any proceeding is brought to foreclose or enforce any lien or encumbrance senior to this Mortgage, Lender may, at its option, pay the amount required to satisfy, discharge, or redeem such senior lien or encumbrance, and all sums so paid shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10.

@H1:ARTICLE 3 — THE LOAN; PAYMENTS; PREPAYMENT
@H2:3.1|The Note and the Note Rate.|The Loan is evidenced by the Note in the original principal amount of $14,750,000.00. The Loan bears interest at a floating rate per annum equal to Daily SOFR plus two hundred eighty-five basis points (2.85%) (the "**Note Rate**"), subject to a floor: in no event shall the SOFR component used in determining the Note Rate be less than three percent (3.00%) per annum. Accordingly, the Note Rate shall in no event be less than five and eighty-five hundredths percent (5.85%) per annum. "**Daily SOFR**" means the Secured Overnight Financing Rate as published by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York (or a successor administrator) on the applicable Business Day, or if such rate is not published on such Business Day, the rate published on the immediately preceding Business Day. The conventions for compounding, lookback, rounding, and business-day adjustment applicable to Daily SOFR shall be as set forth in the Note. If at any time the Note Rate cannot be determined because Daily SOFR is unavailable or is permanently or indefinitely discontinued, the Note Rate shall be determined in accordance with the benchmark replacement provisions of the Note, and Lender and Borrower shall negotiate in good faith any conforming changes to this Mortgage reasonably necessary to give effect to such benchmark replacement.
@H2:3.2|Payment Dates; Maturity.|Accrued interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan shall be due and payable monthly in arrears on the fifteenth (15th) day of each calendar month, commencing May 15, 2025, and on the Maturity Date (each a "**Payment Date**"). The entire outstanding principal balance of the Loan, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and all other amounts due under the Loan Documents, shall be due and payable in full on the Maturity Date, without notice, presentment, or demand, all of which are hereby waived.
@H2:3.3|Interest-Only Period; Amortization.|The Loan shall be interest-only for the first twenty-four (24) months following the Closing Date (the "**Interest-Only Period**"), commencing with the Payment Date occurring on May 15, 2025 and ending on or about April 15, 2027. During the Interest-Only Period, each monthly payment shall consist solely of accrued interest on the outstanding principal balance. Commencing with the Payment Date occurring on May 15, 2027, and continuing through and including the Maturity Date, monthly payments of principal and interest shall be due in amounts sufficient to fully amortize the then-outstanding principal balance over a twenty-five (25) year amortization schedule at the then-applicable Note Rate, with the unpaid principal balance due on the Maturity Date. Following any Advance made after the commencement of amortization, Lender shall recalculate the monthly installment based upon the then-outstanding principal balance, the then-applicable Note Rate, and the remaining amortization period.
@H2:3.4|Default Rate.|Upon the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, the outstanding principal balance of the Loan and, to the extent permitted by Applicable Law, all other amounts due under the Loan Documents, shall bear interest at the Default Rate, being the Note Rate plus five percent (5.00%) per annum. Interest at the Default Rate shall accrue from the date of the occurrence of the Event of Default until such Event of Default is cured or the Debt is paid in full, whichever occurs first, and shall be payable on demand.
@H2:3.5|Late Charge.|If any installment of principal, interest, or other amount due under the Loan Documents is not received by Lender within ten (10) calendar days after its due date, Borrower shall pay to Lender, on demand, a late charge equal to five percent (5.00%) of the overdue amount. The parties agree that such late charge represents a reasonable estimate of the administrative costs and expenses Lender will incur in processing and handling a late payment, is not a penalty, and is in addition to interest at the Default Rate and to all other rights and remedies of Lender.
@H2:3.6|Application of Payments.|All payments received by Lender shall be applied in the following order: first, to late charges; second, to costs, expenses, and protective advances reimbursable to Lender; third, to interest at the Default Rate and interest at the Note Rate; fourth, to principal; and fifth, to any other amounts due. Lender may apply any payment received after the occurrence of an Event of Default in such order as Lender determines. Any payment received after 2:00 p.m. Eastern Time on a Business Day shall be deemed received on the next Business Day.
@H2:3.7|Lockout Period — Absolute Prohibition on Prepayment.|Borrower shall not prepay, and shall not permit any prepayment of, all or any part of the principal balance of the Loan during the period commencing on the Closing Date and ending on the date that is twenty-four (24) months after the Closing Date (the "**Lockout Period**"). Any purported prepayment during the Lockout Period shall be void ab initio, shall not discharge or reduce the Debt, and shall not relieve Borrower of any obligation to make scheduled payments; in addition, any such attempted prepayment shall constitute an Event of Default and a deemed prepayment subject to Section 3.11. No partial prepayment of the Loan is permitted at any time except during the Open Prepayment Period described in Section 3.10.
@H2:3.8|Yield Maintenance Period.|Commencing upon the expiration of the Lockout Period and continuing through the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period (that is, months twenty-five (25) through forty-eight (48) following the Closing Date), Borrower may prepay the Loan in whole (but not in part) upon (a) not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender, which notice shall be irrevocable, and (b) payment, on the date of prepayment, of the entire outstanding principal balance, all accrued and unpaid interest, all other amounts due under the Loan Documents, and the Yield Maintenance Premium.
@H2:3.9|Yield Maintenance Premium.|The "**Yield Maintenance Premium**" payable in connection with any prepayment permitted under Section 3.8 shall equal the greater of:
@I:(a) one percent (1.00%) of the principal amount of the Loan prepaid; and
@I:(b) the present value, as of the date of prepayment, of the excess, if any, of (i) the aggregate amount of interest that would have accrued on the principal amount prepaid from the date of prepayment through the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period at the Note Rate in effect on the date of prepayment, over (ii) the aggregate amount of interest that would accrue on such principal amount over the same period at a rate per annum equal to the Treasury Rate plus fifty (50) basis points (0.50%), with each such amount discounted to present value at the Treasury Rate, calculated on a monthly basis over the number of whole and partial months remaining from the date of prepayment through the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period.
@I:"**Treasury Rate**" means the yield to maturity, as of the second (2nd) Business Day preceding the date of prepayment, of the United States Treasury security having a maturity date closest to, but not exceeding, the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period, as reported in Federal Reserve Statistical Release H.15 (Selected Interest Rates) or any successor publication. If no published maturity exactly matches the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period, the Treasury Rate shall be determined by linear interpolation between the yields of the two published maturities nearest to, one shorter than and one longer than, the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period. If Federal Reserve Statistical Release H.15 is no longer published, the Treasury Rate shall be determined by reference to the yield on the corresponding on-the-run United States Treasury obligation as reported by a nationally recognized pricing service selected by Lender in good faith.
@I:The Yield Maintenance Premium shall be calculated by Lender in good faith using the foregoing formula, and Lender's written calculation, delivered to Borrower together with reasonable supporting detail, shall be conclusive and binding on Borrower absent manifest error. In no event shall the Yield Maintenance Premium be less than zero; however, because the premium equals the greater of the amount described in clause (a) and the amount described in clause (b), the premium payable during the Yield Maintenance Period shall in no event be less than one percent (1.00%) of the principal amount prepaid. **Exhibit D** sets forth a worked illustration of the calculation, which is included for illustrative purposes only and does not modify the operation of this Section 3.9.
@H2:3.10|Open Prepayment Period.|During the period commencing on the first day after the expiration of the Yield Maintenance Period and ending on the Maturity Date (that is, months forty-nine (49) through sixty (60) following the Closing Date), Borrower may prepay the Loan in whole or in part, at any time and from time to time, without payment of any prepayment premium, penalty, or yield maintenance amount, upon not less than fifteen (15) days' prior written notice to Lender. Any partial prepayment shall be applied to the scheduled installments of principal in inverse order of maturity, shall not defer or reduce any scheduled installment, and shall be in a minimum amount of $100,000.00.
@H2:3.11|Involuntary Prepayments; Deemed Prepayments.|(a) If Lender elects to apply casualty insurance proceeds or condemnation awards to the repayment of the Debt in accordance with Section 12.8 or Section 13.3 rather than permitting restoration of the Property, such application shall be made at par without payment of any Yield Maintenance Premium, prepayment premium, or penalty. (b) No Yield Maintenance Premium shall be payable in connection with any prepayment resulting from Lender's acceleration of the Debt following an Event of Default, except where the acceleration follows (i) Borrower's voluntary commencement of a case under the United States Bankruptcy Code or any other insolvency proceeding, or (ii) a voluntary prepayment made in violation of Section 3.7 or Section 3.8, each of which shall be deemed a voluntary prepayment subject to the Yield Maintenance Premium (or, during the Lockout Period, to a premium equal to one percent (1.00%) of the principal amount so prepaid).
@H2:3.12|Usury Savings.|Notwithstanding any other provision of this Mortgage or the Note, no provision of the Loan Documents shall require the payment or permit the collection of interest in excess of the maximum rate permitted by Applicable Law. If any excess interest is provided for or collected, then (a) the amount of interest shall be automatically reduced to the maximum lawful rate, (b) any amount collected in excess of the maximum lawful rate shall be applied to reduce the principal balance of the Loan, and (c) the effective date of the Note shall be automatically reformed to the extent necessary to comply with Applicable Law. To the extent permitted by S.C. Code Ann. § 34-31-20 and other Applicable Law, the parties intend that the Note Rate, the Default Rate, and all other charges be enforceable as agreed.
@H2:3.13|Statements of Account.|Lender shall, upon Borrower's written request not more frequently than once per calendar quarter, deliver a statement of the outstanding principal balance and accrued interest. Lender's books and records shall be presumptive evidence of the amounts due absent manifest error.
