@H1:ARTICLE 4 — ABSOLUTE ASSIGNMENT OF LEASES AND RENTS
@H2:4.1|Absolute and Present Assignment.|Borrower hereby absolutely, presently, and unconditionally transfers, assigns, and sets over to Lender, without reservation and not merely as additional security, all of Borrower's right, title, and interest in, to, and under (a) each and every Lease now existing or hereafter entered into affecting the Property or any part thereof, including all extensions, renewals, amendments, and guaranties thereof; (b) all Rents now or hereafter payable under the Leases or arising from the use or occupancy of the Property; and (c) all rights, powers, privileges, and remedies of Borrower as landlord under the Leases, including the right to enforce payment of Rents, to collect damages for default, to terminate Leases, and to retain and apply security deposits. This assignment is intended to be an absolute assignment of rents within the meaning of the Uniform Assignment of Rents Act as enacted in the State of South Carolina (S.C. Code Ann. § 29-3-100 et seq.), and shall be effective upon execution and recordation of this Mortgage. Borrower represents and warrants that it has not previously assigned, pledged, or encumbered any Lease or any Rents.
@H2:4.2|Perfection; Enforcement Upon Default.|Borrower acknowledges that, under the Uniform Assignment of Rents Act as enacted in South Carolina, Lender's interest in the Rents is perfected upon recordation of this Mortgage in the RMC Office for Charleston County, and that Lender's right to enforce the assignment, including the right to collect Rents directly, arises upon the occurrence of a default by Borrower under the Loan Documents. The parties intend, and Borrower agrees, that an Event of Default under this Mortgage constitutes a default for these purposes, and that Lender may enforce the assignment without the necessity of obtaining a court order, appointing a receiver, taking possession of the Property, or demonstrating that the security is inadequate. Nothing in this Section shall limit Lender's right to seek appointment of a receiver under Section 16.3, and Borrower acknowledges that the availability of the assignment of rents remedy does not preclude the appointment of a receiver, nor does the appointment of a receiver preclude enforcement of the assignment of rents.
@H2:4.3|License to Collect Rents Prior to Default.|Until the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, Borrower shall have a revocable license to collect, retain, and use the Rents in the ordinary course of its business, subject to the terms of the Loan Documents. Such license shall be automatically revoked upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, without further notice, and may be revoked by Lender at any time during the continuance of an Event of Default by written notice to Borrower and, at Lender's election, to the Tenants. Upon revocation, Borrower shall hold all Rents collected thereafter in trust for Lender, shall not commingle such Rents with any other funds, and shall deliver them to Lender within two (2) Business Days of receipt.
@H2:4.4|Notice to Tenants; Direct Collection.|Following an Event of Default, Lender may give written notice (a "**Rent Notice**") to any or all Tenants directing that all Rents thereafter be paid directly to Lender or to a lockbox or account designated by Lender. Borrower shall, within five (5) Business Days after Lender's written request, join in any Rent Notice and take all other actions reasonably requested by Lender to cause the Tenants to pay Rents directly to Lender. Borrower irrevocably appoints Lender as its attorney-in-fact, coupled with an interest, to execute and deliver Rent Notices in Borrower's name and on Borrower's behalf. Each Tenant shall be entitled to rely conclusively on a Rent Notice and shall have no obligation to inquire whether an Event of Default exists; payment of Rents in accordance with a Rent Notice shall discharge such Tenant's obligation to the extent paid.
@H2:4.5|Tenant Estoppel Certificates and SNDAs.|Borrower acknowledges that Lender has required, as a condition precedent to closing under Section 12.1(j) and (k) of the Term Sheet, the delivery of an estoppel certificate and a subordination, non-disturbance, and attornment agreement ("**SNDA**") from each Tenant in occupancy at the Property. Borrower further acknowledges that (a) the Lease with Lowcountry Provisions Inc. contains no provision obligating the Tenant to deliver estoppel certificates and no provision addressing subordination or non-disturbance, and (b) the Leases with Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC and Tidemark Consulting Group LLC require estoppel certificates within fifteen (15) and ten (10) Business Days, respectively, of request. If any estoppel certificate or SNDA is not obtained at or prior to closing, Borrower shall (i) use commercially reasonable efforts, and shall diligently pursue, the delivery of such estoppel certificate and SNDA within thirty (30) days after the Closing Date, and (ii) deliver to Lender monthly written status reports until obtained. Without limiting the foregoing, Borrower shall not be permitted to accept any estoppel certificate or SNDA that contains any qualification or disclosure inconsistent with the Rent Roll or the Leases without Lender's prior written consent, and Borrower shall promptly notify Lender of any such qualification or disclosure.
@H2:4.6|Specific Lease Matters — Lowcountry Provisions Inc.|Borrower represents and warrants that (a) the Lease with Lowcountry Provisions Inc. for Bay 1 (approximately 3,800 square feet) is a triple-net Lease at $28.50 per square foot per annum as of January 1, 2023, subject to annual increases of three percent (3%) effective each January 1, commencing January 1, 2025, and expiring December 31, 2027; (b) such Lease contains no assignment or subletting provision, and specifically contains no consent-to-assignment requirement, prohibition, or landlord approval mechanism; (c) Borrower has the full right, power, and authority to assign all Rents under such Lease and to collaterally and absolutely assign the Lease, and no Tenant consent is required to the assignment effected hereby; and (d) Borrower has not received any notice from such Tenant asserting any claim, offset, or defense in respect of such Lease or the assignment hereof. Borrower shall, within thirty (30) days after the Closing Date, deliver to Lender an estoppel certificate executed by Lowcountry Provisions Inc. acknowledging the existence of this Mortgage, acknowledging the absolute assignment of the Lease and the Rents to Lender, and agreeing to pay Rents to Lender upon written notice following an Event of Default. Borrower shall use commercially reasonable efforts to obtain, at the next renewal, extension, or amendment of such Lease, an amendment adding a customary assignment and subletting consent provision and a customary estoppel and SNDA obligation. Borrower shall not renew, extend, or amend such Lease in any manner inconsistent with this Section 4.6 without Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:4.7|Specific Lease Matters — Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC; Right of First Refusal.|Borrower represents and warrants that (a) the Lease with Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC for Bay 3 (approximately 3,800 square feet) is a modified gross Lease at $24.00 per square foot per annum as of July 1, 2021, subject to annual increases of two and one-half percent (2.5%) effective each July 1, expiring June 30, 2026, and grants the Tenant one (1) three-year renewal option exercisable upon six (6) months' notice (that is, on or before December 31, 2025); (b) such Lease grants the Tenant a right of first refusal (the "**Bay 2 ROFR**") with respect to the leasing of vacant Bay 2 (approximately 3,800 square feet) upon receipt by Borrower of a bona fide third-party offer, exercisable within fifteen (15) Business Days; (c) such Lease contains an early termination right that was exercisable only upon notice delivered on or before December 31, 2024 and that has expired unexercised; and (d) the Bay 2 ROFR survives any renewal of such Lease. Borrower shall (i) comply with the Bay 2 ROFR in good faith and in accordance with its terms in connection with any proposed leasing of Bay 2, (ii) deliver to Lender a copy of any third-party offer and of any ROFR notice delivered to such Tenant, together with evidence of the Tenant's election or non-election, and (iii) not amend, waive, expand, or terminate the Bay 2 ROFR or the renewal option without Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:4.8|Leasing Covenants and Restrictions.|Borrower shall use commercially reasonable efforts to lease all vacant space at the Property at market rents and on terms consistent with those prevailing for comparable mixed-use commercial properties in the Charleston, South Carolina metropolitan area, and on terms reasonably acceptable to Lender. Borrower shall not, without Lender's prior written consent (which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned, or delayed), enter into, renew, extend, or amend any Lease (a) covering more than five thousand (5,000) square feet, (b) having a term (including options to extend) exceeding five (5) years, (c) providing for rent below fair market rent, (d) providing for any rent concession, tenant improvement allowance, or leasing commission not contemplated by the Renovation Budget or the TI/LC Reserve, (e) granting any option to purchase, right of first refusal to purchase, or right of first offer to purchase any portion of the Property, (f) permitting residential use or occupancy of the ground floor of Lot 7, or (g) otherwise materially and adversely affecting the value of the Property or Lender's security. Any Lease made in violation of this Section shall, at Lender's election, constitute an Event of Default. Borrower shall cause each Lease entered into after the Closing Date to be subordinate to this Mortgage and to require the Tenant to execute an SNDA in Lender's customary form upon request. Borrower shall deliver to Lender a copy of each Lease and each Lease modification within ten (10) Business Days after execution.
@H2:4.9|Exclusive Use and Occupancy Restrictions.|Borrower acknowledges that the Lease with Lowcountry Provisions Inc. grants that Tenant an exclusive right to use its premises for the retail sale of specialty grocery and gourmet provisions within the Property, and that such exclusivity may restrict the tenant mix permissible for vacant Bay 2 and Bay 3. Borrower further acknowledges that the LUR prohibits residential use of the ground floor of Lot 7 and that no Lease of any portion of the ground floor of Lot 7 shall permit residential occupancy. Borrower shall not enter into any Lease that violates any exclusive use provision, radius restriction, or other restrictive covenant benefiting an existing Tenant, or that would violate the LUR, without Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:4.10|Security Deposits.|Borrower shall hold all security deposits under the Leases in trust for the Tenants, shall not commingle such deposits with its own funds or with any other funds, and shall maintain records of all such deposits. The aggregate amount of security deposits held by Borrower as of the Closing Date is acknowledged to be $69,183.00. In the event Lender takes possession of the Property or succeeds to Borrower's interest as landlord through foreclosure, deed in lieu, or otherwise, Borrower shall promptly transfer or cause to be transferred to Lender or its designee all security deposits then held, and Lender shall hold such deposits subject to the terms of the applicable Leases. Borrower shall not apply any security deposit to any obligation of a Tenant except in accordance with the applicable Lease and Applicable Law.
@H2:4.11|Subordination of Leases; Non-Disturbance.|Each Lease now or hereafter in effect shall be and is hereby made subject and subordinate to this Mortgage and to all advances made hereunder and all renewals, extensions, and modifications hereof. Lender's obligation to deliver a non-disturbance agreement with respect to any Lease shall be conditioned upon (a) the absence of any Event of Default, (b) receipt of an estoppel certificate from such Tenant in form reasonably satisfactory to Lender, and (c) the Tenant's execution of an SNDA in Lender's customary form, which shall provide, among other things, that so long as the Tenant is not in default beyond applicable notice and cure periods, the Tenant's possession shall not be disturbed by reason of the foreclosure of this Mortgage, and that the Tenant shall attorn to any purchaser at foreclosure.
@H2:4.12|No Liability of Lender; Indemnity.|Lender's acceptance of this assignment does not constitute an assumption by Lender of any obligation of Borrower as landlord under any Lease, and Lender shall have no liability for the performance of any such obligation unless and until Lender takes actual possession of the Property and collects Rents from the Tenants, and then only to the extent of Rents actually collected by Lender. Borrower shall indemnify, defend, and hold Lender harmless from and against all claims, liabilities, losses, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from any act or omission of Borrower as landlord under any Lease, or from any claim that Lender has assumed or is responsible for such obligations.
@H2:4.13|Application of Collected Rents.|All Rents collected by Lender following the revocation of Borrower's license shall be applied in the order set forth in Section 3.6, and Lender shall not be obligated to apply any Rents to the repair, maintenance, or operation of the Property. Lender may, in its discretion, use Rents collected to pay operating expenses of the Property to preserve the value of Lender's security.
