@H1:ARTICLE 5 — REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES
@H2:5.1|General.|Borrower represents and warrants to Lender that each of the following statements is true and correct as of the Closing Date and as of the date of each Advance, and Borrower shall be deemed to have re-made each such representation and warranty as of the date of each Advance.
@H2:5.2|Organization; Power; Authority; Enforceability.|Borrower is a limited liability company duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the State of South Carolina, is qualified to transact business in each jurisdiction in which such qualification is required, and has full power and authority to own, operate, mortgage, and assign the Property and to execute, deliver, and perform this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents. The execution, delivery, and performance of this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents by Borrower have been duly authorized by all requisite limited liability company action, including without limitation the written approval of Members holding not less than seventy-five percent (75%) of the Membership Interests as required by Section 3.2(ii) of the Operating Agreement for any financing of the Property in excess of $1,000,000, and no other consent, approval, or authorization of any Member, manager, or Governmental Authority is required. The person executing this Mortgage on behalf of Borrower, acting through GDG as Managing Member and through Neil Ashford Graydon as sole member and manager of GDG, is duly authorized to do so. This Mortgage and each other Loan Document constitutes the legal, valid, and binding obligation of Borrower, enforceable against Borrower in accordance with its terms, subject to applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, and similar laws and to general principles of equity.
@H2:5.3|No Conflicts.|The execution, delivery, and performance of this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents do not and will not (a) violate any provision of the Operating Agreement, the articles of organization of Borrower, or any other organizational document of Borrower or any Related Entity; (b) conflict with, result in a breach of, or constitute a default under any agreement, instrument, or judgment to which Borrower or any Related Entity is a party or by which the Property is bound, including without limitation the Construction Contract and the Leases; or (c) violate any Applicable Law.
@H2:5.4|Title.|Borrower owns good, marketable, and insurable fee simple title to the Land and the Improvements, and the Liens and security interests created by this Mortgage constitute and will constitute a valid first-priority lien on and security interest in the Property, subject only to the Permitted Exceptions. Borrower has not previously mortgaged, pledged, assigned, or encumbered the Property or any interest therein, and there is no financing statement on file naming Borrower as debtor that covers any portion of the Personal Property.
@H2:5.5|Leases and Rent Roll.|The Rent Roll delivered to Lender is true, correct, and complete in all material respects and identifies each Lease and each Tenant in occupancy. There are no Leases, occupancy agreements, or Tenants other than as reflected on the Rent Roll. The Leases are in full force and effect, no Tenant is more than thirty (30) days in arrears, and no Tenant has asserted any claim, counterclaim, offset, defense, or security interest in any Rents; and no Tenant holds any option to purchase, right of first refusal to purchase, or right of first offer to purchase any portion of the Property. The aggregate security deposits held under the Leases are $69,183.00. Borrower acknowledges that the Rent Roll identifies the in-place annual base rent as $415,100.00 based on the rent rates in effect prior to January 1, 2025 increases, and that the contractual in-place annual base rent as of the Closing Date, giving effect to the escalations provided in the Leases, is approximately $422,966.00, and Borrower shall deliver to Lender at closing a schedule reconciling the two figures.
@H2:5.6|Litigation; Bankruptcy.|There is no action, suit, proceeding, arbitration, or investigation pending or, to Borrower's knowledge, threatened against or affecting Borrower, any Related Entity, Guarantor, or the Property, at law or in equity, that would, if adversely determined, materially and adversely affect the Property, Borrower's ability to perform under the Loan Documents, or the validity or priority of Lender's Liens and security interests. Neither Borrower nor any Related Entity is the subject of any pending or threatened bankruptcy, insolvency, receivership, or similar proceeding, and no such proceeding has been filed by or against Borrower or any Related Entity within the preceding ten (10) years.
@H2:5.7|Environmental Matters.|Except as disclosed in the Phase I ESA, there are no Hazardous Substances located on, under, or emanating from the Property, and there has been no Release of Hazardous Substances at the Property. Borrower has received and reviewed the Phase I ESA and a copy of the LUR and the NFA Letter. The LUR has not been violated, the vapor barrier beneath the ground-floor slab of Bay 1 has not been penetrated, removed, or compromised, and the ground floor of Lot 7 has not been used for residential purposes. Borrower has delivered to Lender all environmental reports, correspondence with SCDHEC, and other environmental records in its possession, custody, or control relating to the Property.
@H2:5.8|Zoning; Compliance.|The Property is located in the GB (General Business) zoning district of the City of Charleston, the current use of the Property as mixed-use retail and office is a permitted use, and neither the Property nor its use violates any Applicable Law, including building, fire, health, safety, and accessibility codes, except for violations that do not and will not materially and adversely affect the Property. All Permits required for the current use and occupancy of the Property have been obtained and are in full force and effect. The Renovation Work, as depicted on the Plans, is permitted under applicable zoning, and Borrower shall obtain all BAR approvals and Permits required for the Renovation Work prior to commencement of the affected work.
@H2:5.9|Single-Purpose Entity.|Borrower is, and at all times during the term of the Loan shall remain, a Single-Purpose Entity in compliance with Article 7. The Operating Agreement, as amended by the Operating Agreement Amendment delivered at closing, contains the Independent Manager requirement, the separateness covenants, the single-purpose restriction, and the unanimity requirement for bankruptcy filings required by Article 7.
@H2:5.10|Solvency; No Fraudulent Transfer.|Borrower is solvent, is not engaged in any business or transaction for which the assets of Borrower are unreasonably small, and does not intend to incur or believe that it will incur debts beyond its ability to pay as they become due. The Loan is being made for reasonably equivalent value, and Borrower has not entered into the Loan Documents with any intent to hinder, delay, or defraud any creditor.
@H2:5.11|OFAC; Anti-Terrorism; Beneficial Ownership.|Neither Borrower, any Related Entity, Guarantor, nor any of their respective beneficial owners is a Person named on the Specially Designated Nationals and Blocked Persons List maintained by OFAC or otherwise subject to any sanctions administered by OFAC, nor is any such Person owned or controlled by any such Person. Borrower has delivered to Lender all certifications of beneficial ownership and identifying information required by Lender's customer due diligence and anti-money-laundering policies.
@H2:5.12|Insurance.|Borrower has obtained, and shall maintain in full force and effect, all insurance required by Article 12. The insurance policies name Lender as mortgagee, loss payee, and/or additional insured as applicable and will not be cancelled, materially modified, or non-renewed without at least thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender.
@H2:5.13|Construction Contract; Renovation Budget.|Borrower has delivered to Lender a true, correct, and complete copy of the executed Construction Contract, including all schedules and exhibits, which is in the contract sum of $2,850,000.00 and is in full force and effect. No default by Borrower or the General Contractor exists under the Construction Contract, and no change order has been executed. The Renovation Budget is an accurate estimate of the total cost of completing the Renovation Work, and the sources of funding for the Renovation Work described on **Exhibit C** are available and committed.
@H2:5.14|Condition of the Property.|The Improvements were originally constructed in 1952 and were substantially renovated in 2004. Borrower acknowledges that Lender has relied upon the appraisal of the Property prepared by Pinnacle Valuation Services LLC dated February 14, 2025 (File No. PVS-2025-0214-CHS) and the Phase I ESA, and that no representation is made by Lender as to the physical condition or value of the Property. Borrower accepts the Property in its "as-is" condition, subject to the completion of the Renovation Work.
@H2:5.15|Accuracy of Information.|All information, reports, financial statements, and other data furnished by or on behalf of Borrower or Guarantor to Lender in connection with the Loan, including the information set forth in the Term Sheet and in the Rent Roll, are true, correct, and complete in all material respects and do not contain any material misstatement of fact or omit to state any material fact necessary to make the statements contained therein not misleading.
@H2:5.16|Survival.|The representations and warranties set forth in this Article 5 shall survive the closing, the making of the Loan, and the recording of this Mortgage, and shall continue until the Debt is paid and performed in full.

@H1:ARTICLE 6 — AFFIRMATIVE COVENANTS
@H2:6.1|Payment of the Debt.|Borrower shall pay and perform the Debt when due, whether at stated maturity, by acceleration, or otherwise, without offset, counterclaim, abatement, or deduction of any kind.
@H2:6.2|Impositions.|Borrower shall pay and discharge, before the same become delinquent, all Impositions and all other charges, liens, and encumbrances affecting the Property or any part thereof, including without limitation real property taxes on all three tax parcels. Borrower shall deposit monthly with Lender the amounts required under Section 11.1 for the payment of real property taxes and insurance premiums. Borrower may contest any Imposition in good faith by appropriate proceedings diligently conducted, provided that (a) Borrower has deposited with Lender such reserve as Lender reasonably requires to protect its interest, (b) no lien is enforced against the Property during such contest, and (c) Borrower promptly notifies Lender of the commencement and resolution of such contest.
@H2:6.3|Insurance.|Borrower shall obtain and maintain, at its sole cost and expense, all insurance required by Article 12, shall pay all premiums therefor when due, and shall deliver evidence of coverage to Lender in accordance with Section 12.7.
@H2:6.4|Maintenance and Repairs; No Waste.|Borrower shall keep and maintain the Property, including all Improvements, fixtures, building systems, and common areas, in good order, condition, and repair, and in a condition consistent with the standards applicable to comparable mixed-use commercial properties in the Charleston, South Carolina metropolitan area. Borrower shall promptly make all repairs, replacements, and renewals necessary to preserve the value and rentability of the Property, and shall not commit or permit any waste of the Property or any portion thereof. Borrower shall not remove, demolish, or materially alter any Improvement without Lender's prior written consent, except for the Renovation Work performed in accordance with Article 10.
@H2:6.5|Compliance with Laws.|Borrower shall at all times comply with all Applicable Law affecting the Property or the conduct of Borrower's business, including without limitation all zoning, building, fire, health, safety, accessibility, and environmental laws and regulations, and all conditions of the Permits and any encroachment license or agreement with the City of Charleston relating to the decorative iron balcony over the King Street right-of-way. Borrower shall maintain the balcony encroachment in compliance with any permit, license, or encroachment agreement obtained from the City of Charleston and shall promptly notify Lender of any notice from the City of Charleston concerning such encroachment, including any notice requiring removal, alteration, or the obtaining of a permit.
@H2:6.6|Books and Records; Financial Reporting.|Borrower shall keep and maintain complete and accurate books and records of account in accordance with GAAP, and shall deliver to Lender the financial statements, reports, rent rolls, compliance certificates, and other information required by Article 14.
@H2:6.7|Leasing Efforts.|Borrower shall use commercially reasonable efforts to lease the vacant space at the Property (comprising Bay 2 and 2nd Floor Suite B, totaling approximately 13,600 square feet) at market rents and on terms consistent with Section 4.8, and shall deliver to Lender quarterly written reports describing the status of leasing efforts, including all offers received and the status of the Bay 2 ROFR process. Borrower acknowledges that the as-stabilized value of the Property and the satisfaction of the DSCR covenant depend upon the lease-up of such space, and Borrower shall not withdraw or materially reduce its leasing efforts without Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:6.8|Reserves.|Borrower shall make the deposits to the Reserve Accounts required by Article 11 and shall comply with the conditions to disbursement from each Reserve Account.
@H2:6.9|Completion of the Renovation Work.|Borrower shall diligently prosecute the Renovation Work to Substantial Completion in accordance with the Plans, on or before the Substantial Completion Deadline of June 15, 2026, and within the Renovation Budget. Borrower shall fund from its own funds, and not from the proceeds of the Loan, all costs of the Renovation Work in excess of (a) the Renovation Holdback and (b) the amount allocated to Borrower's equity contribution for the Renovation Work on **Exhibit C**. Borrower shall not permit any stoppage of Renovation Work for more than twenty (20) consecutive days, except for events of Force Majeure approved in writing by Lender, not to exceed an aggregate of sixty (60) days.
@H2:6.10|Environmental Compliance.|Borrower shall comply with Article 9 and with all Environmental Laws and all institutional controls applicable to the Property.
@H2:6.11|Further Assurances; Title and Perfection.|Borrower shall, at its sole cost and expense, execute, acknowledge, deliver, record, and file such further instruments, financing statements, continuation statements, fixture filings, affidavits, and certificates as Lender may reasonably request to confirm, perfect, or preserve the Liens, security interests, and assignment created hereby, and to cause the Title Insurer to issue each endorsement required by Lender, including without limitation a zoning endorsement, an access endorsement, a survey endorsement, a comprehensive endorsement, a future advance endorsement, and, to the extent available on commercially reasonable terms, an ALTA 28.1 (encroachments) endorsement and affirmative coverage with respect to the vacated Anson Lane strip. Borrower shall deliver to Lender, within thirty (30) days after closing, the final Title Policy with all endorsements. Borrower shall promptly deliver to Lender copies of all title date-down endorsements obtained during the Renovation Work.
@H2:6.12|Taxes and Recording; Documentary Stamp Tax.|Borrower shall pay all recording fees, documentary stamp taxes, mortgage registration taxes, and other charges payable in connection with the recording of this Mortgage, including the South Carolina documentary stamp tax on the indebtedness secured hereby. Borrower shall pay any additional documentary stamp tax payable upon any Advance made after the Closing Date, if and to the extent required by Applicable Law.
@H2:6.13|Notices to Lender.|Borrower shall deliver written notice to Lender within five (5) Business Days after Borrower obtains knowledge of (a) any Event of Default or any event that, with notice or lapse of time or both, would constitute an Event of Default; (b) any litigation, arbitration, or governmental proceeding commenced against or affecting Borrower, any Related Entity, Guarantor, or the Property that involves a claim in excess of $50,000; (c) any Release of Hazardous Substances, any notice or order from SCDHEC or any other Governmental Authority relating to the Property or the LUR, or any correspondence with SCDHEC relating to Site ID No. SC-29403-0772; (d) any casualty, condemnation, or other damage to or taking of the Property; (e) any default by a Tenant under any Lease, any notice of termination or material dispute from any Tenant, and any bankruptcy filing by any Tenant; (f) any default under the Construction Contract, any stop-work order, any mechanic's or materialman's lien, or any notice of nonpayment from the General Contractor or any subcontractor; (g) any change in the identity of the registered agent, the principal office, the name, or the organizational identification number of Borrower; and (h) any change in the ownership or control of Borrower, any Related Entity, or Guarantor.
@H2:6.14|Inspection; Access.|Lender, its agents, employees, appraisers, engineers, inspectors, and consultants shall have the right, upon not less than one (1) Business Day's prior notice (or without notice following an Event of Default) and during reasonable business hours, to enter upon and inspect the Property and to examine and copy Borrower's books and records relating to the Property. Lender shall use commercially reasonable efforts to conduct inspections in a manner that does not unreasonably interfere with the operation of the Property or the Renovation Work and, except in an emergency or following an Event of Default, shall not conduct more than four (4) such inspections in any twelve-month period without Borrower's consent. Lender shall not be deemed to be a mortgagee in possession or to have assumed control of the Property by reason of any inspection.
@H2:6.15|Lien Protection; Notices of Nonresponsibility.|Borrower shall pay when due all claims for labor, services, and materials furnished to the Property, and shall keep the Property free from any mechanic's or materialman's lien, judgment lien, or other encumbrance except Permitted Exceptions. If any such lien is filed, Borrower shall discharge it of record, by payment or by bonding, within thirty (30) days after receipt of notice thereof. With respect to any tenant improvement work performed for a Tenant at the Property, Borrower shall, within the time permitted by S.C. Code Ann. § 29-5-20, post and record (if applicable) a Notice of Nonresponsibility in the form required by South Carolina law, and shall deliver a copy thereof to Lender within five (5) Business Days after posting. Borrower shall cause all construction contracts and subcontracts relating to the Renovation Work to provide for lien waivers in accordance with Section 10.5 and shall not authorize or permit any construction work to commence prior to the recording of this Mortgage.
@H2:6.16|Borrower Estoppel Certificates.|Within ten (10) Business Days after Lender's written request, Borrower shall deliver a written estoppel certificate confirming the outstanding principal balance, accrued interest, the absence or existence of defaults, the validity and priority of the Loan Documents, and such other matters as Lender may reasonably request. Borrower authorizes Lender to rely conclusively on any such certificate and to deliver it to any assignee or participant of Lender.
@H2:6.17|Cooperation with Lender's Consultants.|Borrower shall cooperate with, and shall cause the General Contractor, the Architect, and its other consultants to cooperate with, any appraiser, environmental consultant, inspector, or other consultant retained by Lender, and shall pay the reasonable cost of such consultants to the extent required by Section 13.2 of the Term Sheet.
@H2:6.18|Affiliate Agreements Subordinated.|All management fees, development fees, asset management fees, construction management fees, and other compensation payable by Borrower to GDG or to any other Affiliate or Member, whether under the Operating Agreement or otherwise, shall be subordinate to the prior payment in full of the Debt and shall not be paid at any time during which an Event of Default exists or during which the DSCR is less than 1.25x. Borrower shall cause each such agreement to be amended accordingly prior to the Closing Date and shall deliver a copy to Lender.
@H2:6.19|Compliance with Guaranty and Environmental Indemnity.|Borrower shall cause Guarantor to comply with each of its obligations under the Guaranty and the Environmental Indemnity, and any failure of Guarantor to so comply shall constitute an Event of Default hereunder.
