@H1:ARTICLE 7 — SINGLE-PURPOSE ENTITY, SEPARATENESS, AND BANKRUPTCY REMOTENESS
@H2:7.1|Single-Purpose Entity.|Borrower shall at all times maintain its status as a single-purpose entity (an "**SPE**" or "**Single-Purpose Entity**"). Without limiting the foregoing, Borrower shall not engage in any business or activity other than the acquisition, ownership, operation, renovation, leasing, management, financing, and disposition of the Property and activities incidental thereto, and Borrower's sole purpose shall be limited to the foregoing. Borrower shall not, and shall cause the Members not to, amend or interpret the purpose clause of the Operating Agreement to permit any activity beyond such single purpose.
@H2:7.2|Separateness Covenants.|Borrower shall at all times, and shall cause each Related Entity to take all actions necessary to ensure that Borrower shall:
@I:(a) maintain its own separate books of account, financial records, bank accounts, and records, separate and apart from those of any other Person;
@I:(b) not commingle its funds or assets with those of any Affiliate, Member, manager, or other Person, and not permit its assets to be used for the purposes of any other Person;
@I:(c) hold itself out to the public, and conduct its business, under its own name, and use its own stationery, invoices, checks, and business forms;
@I:(d) observe all customary organizational formalities, including maintaining minutes and records of the actions of its Members and Managing Member, and not commingle its affairs with those of any Member;
@I:(e) pay its own liabilities and obligations from its own assets, and not guarantee or become obligated for the debts of any Affiliate or Member;
@I:(f) maintain arm's-length relationships with all Affiliates and Members, and enter into transactions with Affiliates only on commercially reasonable terms disclosed to Lender;
@I:(g) not pledge its assets for the benefit of any other Person, and not make any loans or advances to any Affiliate or Member;
@I:(h) maintain adequate capitalization in light of its contemplated business operations, transactions, and liabilities, and not distribute assets in a manner that would leave it inadequately capitalized;
@I:(i) not acquire obligations or securities of, or make any investment in, any Affiliate or Member;
@I:(j) correctly and consistently identify itself as a separate legal entity in all correspondence, contracts, and public filings, and not misrepresent its identity or its relationship to any Member or Affiliate; and
@I:(k) file its own tax returns and pay its own taxes, if any, required to be filed or paid by it.
@H2:7.3|Independent Manager.|Borrower shall maintain at all times at least one (1) Independent Manager whose affirmative vote or written consent is required, and without which Borrower shall not be authorized, to (a) file a voluntary petition under the United States Bankruptcy Code or under any state insolvency or receivership law, (b) consent to, acquiesce in, or fail to contest the appointment of a receiver, trustee, or custodian, or the entry of an order for relief in any involuntary case, (c) dissolve, liquidate, wind up, or terminate its existence, (d) merge or consolidate with any Person, (e) sell, convey, or otherwise dispose of all or substantially all of its assets, or (f) make an assignment for the benefit of creditors or admit in writing its inability to pay its debts generally as they become due. Such Independent Manager shall be appointed in accordance with the Operating Agreement as amended by the Operating Agreement Amendment, and shall not be removed without the prior written consent of Lender or contemporaneous appointment of a successor Independent Manager meeting the definition hereof. Borrower shall cause the Independent Manager to be bound by the fiduciary duties of care and loyalty to Borrower and, to the extent permitted by law, to consider the interests of Lender in exercising the authority described in this Section.
@H2:7.4|No Voluntary Bankruptcy Without Independent Manager Consent.|Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of Lender and the affirmative vote or written consent of the Independent Manager, commence any case or proceeding under the United States Bankruptcy Code or any other federal or state insolvency law, or consent to or acquiesce in any such filing. Borrower acknowledges that this Section is intended, among other things, to render Borrower bankruptcy remote and to protect the value of Lender's security, and that Lender is relying materially thereon in making the Loan. Borrower shall not, and shall cause the Members not to, take any action to remove, replace, or circumvent the Independent Manager for the purpose of facilitating any such filing.
@H2:7.5|Covenants Binding on Members.|Borrower acknowledges that Lender is relying upon the covenants set forth in this Article 7 and that such covenants must be binding upon the Members, and not only upon the Managing Member. Borrower shall cause each Member (including, in the case of Tidewater, Tidewater GP Holdings LLC as its general partner, and, in the case of Harborline, each of its managing members) to execute and deliver at closing a joinder or consent to the Operating Agreement Amendment and to any other instrument reasonably required by Lender to evidence their agreement to be bound by the provisions of this Article 7 and by the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 8.1.
@H2:7.6|Operating Agreement Amendment; No Amendment of SPE Provisions.|As a condition precedent to closing, Borrower shall deliver to Lender an executed amendment to the Operating Agreement (the "**Operating Agreement Amendment**"), executed by all three Members, which shall (a) add the Independent Manager requirement described in Section 7.3, (b) add the separateness covenants described in Section 7.2, (c) narrow the purpose clause to the single-purpose restriction described in Section 7.1, (d) require the unanimous written consent of all Members and the Independent Manager for any voluntary bankruptcy filing, dissolution, merger, or consolidation, (e) provide that the Member approval required for Major Decisions shall not be amended without Lender's prior written consent, and (f) provide that no amendment of the foregoing provisions shall be effective without Lender's prior written consent. Borrower shall not amend, modify, waive, or repeal any SPE provision of the Operating Agreement, or any provision of the Operating Agreement Amendment, without Lender's prior written consent in each instance (which consent may be withheld in Lender's sole discretion), and Borrower shall deliver to Lender a copy of each amendment to the Operating Agreement within five (5) Business Days after its execution.
@H2:7.7|Key Principal; Change of Control.|Borrower acknowledges that Lender has relied upon the personal creditworthiness, experience, and management of Neil Ashford Graydon as the Guarantor and as the sole member and manager of GDG, the Managing Member of Borrower ("**Key Principal**"). Borrower shall cause the Key Principal to retain, directly or indirectly, sole control of GDG and, through GDG, of the day-to-day management of Borrower, and shall not permit any change in the direct or indirect ownership or control of GDG, or any change in the identity of the Managing Member of Borrower, without Lender's prior written consent in each instance.
@H2:7.8|Member and Affiliate Agreements Subordinate; Drag-Along.|Borrower shall cause the Operating Agreement, and any other agreement among the Members or between Borrower and any Member or Affiliate, to be expressly subordinate to the Loan Documents, such that (a) no right of any Member to consent to, participate in, or participate in the proceeds of any sale, transfer, or financing of the Property may be exercised in a manner that violates Article 8, and (b) the drag-along rights described in Section 4.4 of the Operating Agreement (which, as summarized, may permit Members holding eighty percent (80%) or more of the Membership Interests to require all other Members to participate in a sale of the Property) may not be exercised unless Lender has consented in writing to the related transfer in accordance with Section 8.1.
@H2:7.9|Consequence of Breach.|Any breach of any covenant set forth in this Article 7 shall constitute an immediate Event of Default, without notice and without any opportunity to cure, as provided in Section 15.3(c).

@H1:ARTICLE 8 — NEGATIVE COVENANTS AND TRANSFER RESTRICTIONS
