@I:(c) The restrictions in this Section 8.1 extend to indirect and upstream transfers and to changes of control. Any change in the direct or indirect ownership or control of any Member, of any Person that controls any Member, or of GDG (including without limitation any sale or transfer of Neil Ashford Graydon's direct or indirect interest in GDG, any acquisition, merger, or replacement of Tidewater GP Holdings LLC as general partner of Tidewater, any transfer of Tidewater's interest to a "successor fund" or Affiliate of Tidewater GP Holdings LLC under Section 4.2(c) of the Operating Agreement, and any change in the membership or management of Harborline) shall constitute a transfer for purposes of this Section 8.1 and shall require Lender's prior written consent, notwithstanding that no direct transfer of a Membership Interest in Borrower may occur.
@I:(d) Any transfer made in violation of this Section 8.1 shall be void ab initio, shall constitute an immediate Event of Default without notice or opportunity to cure, and shall constitute a full recourse carve-out event under Section 17.2.
@H2:8.2|No Subordinate or Additional Financing.|Borrower shall not incur, create, assume, guarantee, or permit to exist any indebtedness, secured or unsecured, for borrowed money, any subordinate lien, mortgage, or security interest in the Property, or any mezzanine loan, preferred equity interest, or other financing arrangement that may affect Lender's collateral position, without Lender's prior written consent, which consent may be withheld in Lender's sole discretion.
@H2:8.3|No Other Liens or Encumbrances.|Borrower shall not create, incur, assume, or permit to exist any lien, mortgage, deed of trust, pledge, security interest, charge, easement (other than the Permitted Exceptions), restriction, covenant, or other encumbrance on the Property or any portion thereof.
@H2:8.4|No Change in Use, Zoning, or Improvement.|Borrower shall not (a) change the use of the Property from mixed-use retail and office, (b) seek or consent to any change in the zoning classification of the Property, (c) permit any residential use or occupancy of any portion of the Property, (d) demolish or structurally alter any Improvement other than in connection with the Renovation Work, (e) record any subdivision or condominium plat, or (f) grant any option, right of first refusal, or right of first offer with respect to the Property.
@H2:8.5|No Amendments to Material Agreements.|Borrower shall not amend, modify, terminate, or waive any material right under the Construction Contract, any Project Document, any Lease (except as permitted by Section 4.8), the Operating Agreement (except as permitted by Section 7.6), or any agreement with an Affiliate, without Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:8.6|No Dissolution, Merger, or Change in Structure.|Borrower shall not dissolve, liquidate, wind up, merge, consolidate, or convert its organizational form, and shall not change its fiscal year, its method of accounting, its name, its state of organization, its federal employer identification number, or its registered agent, in each case without Lender's prior written consent (with respect to a change of name, state of organization, or organizational identification number, Lender's consent may not be unreasonably withheld but Borrower shall give not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice so that Lender may file protective UCC amendments).
