@H2:9.1|General Environmental Covenants.|Borrower shall (a) comply, and cause all Tenants and occupants of the Property to comply, with all Environmental Laws; (b) not cause or permit any Release of Hazardous Substances at, on, under, or from the Property; (c) not store, use, generate, treat, or dispose of any Hazardous Substances at the Property except customary cleaning supplies and de minimis quantities used in the ordinary operation and maintenance of a mixed-use commercial building; (d) obtain and maintain all environmental permits required for the operation of the Property; and (e) promptly notify Lender of any Release, any notice or order from any Governmental Authority relating to Hazardous Substances, and any claim or demand relating to environmental conditions at the Property.
@H2:9.2|Acknowledgment of the Phase I ESA, the CREC, and the NFA Letter.|Lender and Borrower acknowledge that the Phase I ESA identifies no Recognized Environmental Conditions and one Controlled Recognized Environmental Condition affecting the southwest corner of Lot 7, arising from historical dry-cleaning operations at the adjacent property located at 518 King Street, which contamination was addressed under SCDHEC oversight and is the subject of the NFA Letter and the LUR. Borrower shall (a) obtain and deliver to Lender at or prior to closing; and (b) maintain at the Property and make available to Lender upon request, a complete copy of the SCDHEC file for Site ID No. SC-29403-0772, including all sampling data, remediation reports, groundwater monitoring results, and the NFA Letter with all conditions and attachments.
@H2:9.3|Land Use Restriction — Specific Covenants.|Borrower acknowledges that the LUR runs with the land, is binding upon Borrower and all Tenants and successors in interest to Lot 7, and is enforceable by SCDHEC. Without limiting Section 9.1, Borrower shall:
@I:(a) not use, permit the use of, or lease any portion of the ground floor of Lot 7 (comprising approximately 3,800 square feet and commonly known as Bay 1, 520 King Street) for residential purposes, or for any use inconsistent with the LUR;
@I:(b) maintain in good condition and working order, at its sole cost, the vapor barrier system installed beneath the concrete floor slab of Bay 1, and not penetrate, remove, damage, compromise, or render ineffective such vapor barrier without the prior written approval of SCDHEC and the prior written consent of Lender;
@I:(c) cause the vapor barrier to be inspected at least annually, and prior to and following any Renovation Work or other construction, demolition, or alteration activity affecting the floor slab of Bay 1, by a licensed environmental professional or licensed engineer reasonably acceptable to Lender, and deliver a written report of each such inspection to Lender within thirty (30) days after completion of the inspection;
@I:(d) notify SCDHEC in writing in advance of any Renovation Work or other activity that may penetrate, alter, or affect the floor slab of Bay 1 or the vapor barrier, and deliver a copy of such notice to Lender not less than five (5) Business Days prior to delivery to SCDHEC;
@I:(e) notify the General Contractor, the Architect, and each subcontractor performing work at or near Bay 1, in writing and before commencement of their work, of the existence and location of the vapor barrier and of the requirements of the LUR, and deliver a copy of each such notice to Lender;
@I:(f) deliver to Lender, within five (5) Business Days after receipt or delivery, copies of all correspondence, notices, reports, inspection results, and orders relating to the LUR, the vapor barrier, or Site ID No. SC-29403-0772;
@I:(g) not modify, amend, terminate, release, or seek the modification, amendment, termination, or release of the LUR, and not consent to any such action, without Lender's prior written consent in each instance;
@I:(h) maintain all institutional controls required by the NFA Letter and the LUR, and record any instrument required by SCDHEC to maintain such controls, and provide Lender with evidence of recording;
@I:(i) if SCDHEC requires additional investigation, monitoring, remediation, or regulatory action with respect to the Property, perform the same diligently at Borrower's sole cost and expense and deliver copies of all related work plans and reports to Lender; and
@I:(j) take all "reasonable steps" and exercise "appropriate care" with respect to Hazardous Substances at the Property as required to preserve and maintain the protections afforded by CERCLA to a bona fide prospective purchaser and a contiguous property owner under 42 U.S.C. § 9607(p) and (q) and 40 C.F.R. Part 312, and cooperate with Lender in maintaining Lender's own rights to such protections, including Lender's rights as a secured creditor under 42 U.S.C. § 9601(20)(E).
@H2:9.4|Tenant Compliance; Lease Provisions.|Borrower shall cause each Lease affecting any portion of the ground floor of Lot 7 to (a) prohibit residential use and occupancy of the premises, (b) prohibit any penetration of or alteration to the floor slab of Bay 1 without the landlord's prior written consent and without compliance with the LUR and SCDHEC requirements, (c) require the Tenant to comply with the LUR, and (d) require the Tenant to permit the landlord and its agents to enter to inspect and maintain the vapor barrier. Borrower shall deliver a copy of the LUR to each Tenant of any portion of the ground floor of Lot 7. Borrower shall promptly notify Lender of any act or omission of any Tenant that may constitute a violation of the LUR.
