@H1:ARTICLE 10 — RENOVATION WORK AND DISBURSEMENT OF THE RENOVATION HOLDBACK
@H2:10.1|Renovation Work; Plans; Permits; Construction Contract.|Borrower shall cause the Renovation Work to be performed diligently and in a good and workmanlike manner, in accordance with the Plans, the Renovation Budget, the Construction Contract, and all Applicable Law. Borrower shall obtain all Permits required for the Renovation Work, including without limitation all BAR approvals for the façade restoration, and shall deliver copies of all Permits to Lender prior to commencement of the affected work. The general contractor for the Renovation Work shall be Beaufort Builders Group LLC, South Carolina General Contractor License No. SC-GC-47921, pursuant to the Construction Contract in the contract sum of $2,850,000.00 covering hard costs of construction. Borrower shall deliver to Lender a complete copy of the executed Construction Contract, together with all schedules, exhibits, and amendments, prior to closing. Borrower shall not replace the General Contractor, and shall not materially amend, terminate, or waive any material right under the Construction Contract, without Lender's prior written consent. Any architectural, engineering, or construction management agreement relating to the Renovation Work shall be in form and substance reasonably acceptable to Lender, and Borrower shall cause each such agreement to contain customary certifications, lien waivers, and insurance requirements.
@H2:10.2|Renovation Budget; Overruns.|The Renovation Budget is $3,150,000.00, allocated among the line items described on **Exhibit C**, of which $2,250,000.00 is to be funded from the Renovation Holdback and $900,000.00 from Borrower's equity contribution. Borrower shall pay, from its own funds and not from the proceeds of the Loan, all costs of the Renovation Work in excess of the Renovation Budget and all costs of the Renovation Work not specifically included in the Renovation Budget. Any change in the Renovation Budget, and any reallocation among line items exceeding ten percent (10%) of the affected line item, requires Lender's prior written consent.
@H2:10.3|Substantial Completion Deadline.|Borrower shall achieve Substantial Completion of the Renovation Work on or before June 15, 2026 (the Substantial Completion Deadline), being fourteen (14) months after the Closing Date. Borrower's failure to achieve Substantial Completion on or before such date shall constitute an Event of Default, subject to extension only for delays caused by Force Majeure (as defined in Section 10.17) not to exceed an aggregate of sixty (60) days and only if Borrower has delivered written notice to Lender within ten (10) days after the commencement of such delay and has diligently pursued completion. Borrower shall deliver to Lender, within ten (10) days after Substantial Completion, (a) the Architect's certificate of Substantial Completion, (b) the certificate of occupancy or equivalent final inspection approval for the renovated portions of the Property, and (c) a certificate of Borrower as to the final cost of the Renovation Work.
@H2:10.4|The Renovation Holdback.|Lender shall make the Renovation Holdback available to Borrower in Advances for the payment of hard and soft costs of the Renovation Work, subject to the conditions of this Article 10. The Renovation Holdback is not a revolving facility; amounts repaid or unused may not be re-borrowed, and any portion of the Renovation Holdback not disbursed by the date that is eighteen (18) months after the Closing Date shall be cancelled and shall no longer be available to Borrower.
@H2:10.5|Conditions to Each Advance.|Lender's obligation to make any Advance from the Renovation Holdback is subject to the satisfaction of each of the following conditions, in Lender's reasonable judgment:
@I:(a) no Event of Default, and no event that with notice or lapse of time or both would constitute an Event of Default, shall have occurred and be continuing;
@I:(b) Borrower shall have delivered a written draw request to Lender not less than ten (10) Business Days prior to the requested disbursement date, in the form of **Exhibit E**, together with an AIA G702/G703 Application and Certificate for Payment certified by the Architect, detailing the work completed, amounts previously paid, and the amount currently requested;
@I:(c) the Architect shall have certified the percentage of completion of the work for which payment is requested and that such work has been performed in accordance with the Plans;
@I:(d) Borrower shall have delivered conditional lien waivers for the current draw and unconditional lien waivers for all prior draws from the General Contractor and each subcontractor or supplier performing work or furnishing materials in an amount exceeding $25,000, in each case in form reasonably satisfactory to Lender and the Title Insurer;
@I:(e) the Title Insurer shall have issued a date-down endorsement confirming that no mechanic's or materialman's lien or other intervening lien or encumbrance has been filed against the Property since the date of this Mortgage or the most recent date-down endorsement, and confirming that the Title Policy remains in full force and effect;
@I:(f) Lender shall have received evidence of a satisfactory inspection of the work in progress, which inspection may be conducted by a third-party inspector retained by Lender at Borrower's expense, and which Borrower shall permit within five (5) Business Days after the draw request;
@I:(g) the aggregate equity contributions made by Borrower to the cost of the Renovation Work shall not be less than twenty-eight and fifty-seven hundredths percent (28.57%) of the aggregate cost of the Renovation Work funded to date (including the requested Advance), such that Borrower's equity is contributed on a not-less-than-ratable basis with the Renovation Holdback, and Borrower shall deliver evidence of each such equity contribution;
@I:(h) all Permits and BAR approvals required for the work covered by the draw request shall have been obtained, and all work shall have been performed in compliance with Applicable Law;
@I:(i) with respect to any work affecting Bay 1 or the floor slab of Bay 1, Borrower shall have satisfied each of the requirements of Section 9.3, including the pre-work vapor barrier inspection and the prior written notice to SCDHEC; and
@I:(j) the Construction Contract shall be in full force and effect, and no default or stop-work order shall be outstanding.
@H2:10.6|Retainage.|Lender shall withhold from each Advance from the Renovation Holdback an amount equal to ten percent (10%) of the work in place covered by such Advance (the "**Retainage**") until Substantial Completion has been achieved in accordance with Section 10.3. Lender shall release the Retainage upon Lender's receipt of (a) the Architect's certificate of Substantial Completion, (b) final unconditional lien waivers from the General Contractor and all subcontractors and suppliers, (c) a final title date-down endorsement, (d) the certificate of occupancy or equivalent final approval, and (e) evidence that all punch-list items have been completed or are bonded or escrowed to Lender's satisfaction. No interest shall accrue on the Retainage. The aggregate Retainage may not exceed ten percent (10%) of the Renovation Holdback ($225,000.00).
@H2:10.7|Manner of Disbursement.|Lender may disburse each Advance (a) to Borrower, (b) directly to the General Contractor, the Architect, or any other contractor or consultant, or (c) through the Title Insurer or a disbursing agent, in each case as Lender determines in its reasonable discretion to protect its interests and to obtain the lien waivers and title date-downs required hereby. Borrower hereby authorizes Lender to make disbursements directly to third parties and acknowledges that such disbursements shall constitute Advances to Borrower and shall be secured by this Mortgage.
@H2:10.8|Change Orders.|Borrower shall not approve or permit any change order, construction change directive, or field order affecting the Renovation Work that (a) exceeds $50,000.00 individually or $150,000.00 in the aggregate, (b) affects the structural, mechanical, electrical, elevator, HVAC, or façade systems, (c) is inconsistent with the Plans or the approved scope, or (d) would cause the total cost of the Renovation Work to exceed the Renovation Budget, without Lender's prior written consent. Borrower shall deliver to Lender a copy of each executed change order within five (5) Business Days after execution.
@H2:10.9|Borrower's Equity Contribution.|Borrower shall contribute not less than $900,000.00 of its own funds toward the cost of the Renovation Work, in accordance with the funding allocation set forth on **Exhibit C** and on a schedule not less favorable to Lender than the draw schedule delivered to Lender at closing. Borrower acknowledges that the draw schedule delivered to Lender at closing reflects the expenditure of Borrower's equity on a basis that is not strictly ratable with the Renovation Holdback in the first two draws, and Borrower shall ensure that by the date of the fifth Advance its aggregate equity contributions equal not less than 28.57% of total Renovation Work costs funded to date.
@H2:10.10|Completion Guaranty; Cost Overruns.|Guarantor has executed and delivered the Completion Guaranty, pursuant to which Guarantor unconditionally guarantees the completion of the Renovation Work in accordance with the Plans, within the Renovation Budget, and on or before the Substantial Completion Deadline. Borrower acknowledges and agrees that the Completion Guaranty is not capped by the amount of the Renovation Budget or the Renovation Holdback, and that Guarantor shall be obligated to fund all costs of completion of the Renovation Work, including costs in excess of the Renovation Budget, regardless of the cause of such excess. Borrower shall promptly advance to itself or to the General Contractor, as applicable, any funds required to complete the Renovation Work upon demand by Lender.
@H2:10.11|Lender's Right to Complete.|If (a) an Event of Default has occurred and is continuing, (b) Borrower fails to achieve Substantial Completion by the Substantial Completion Deadline, or (c) Borrower abandons or suspends the Renovation Work for more than twenty (20) consecutive days (other than as permitted by Section 6.9), then Lender may, at its option and without obligation to do so, (i) enter upon the Property, (ii) take possession of all materials, equipment, and plans, (iii) employ architects, contractors, and consultants, (iv) complete or cause the completion of the Renovation Work, and (v) pay, settle, or compromise any claims relating thereto. All amounts so expended by Lender, together with interest at the Default Rate, shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10, shall be secured by this Mortgage, and shall be immediately due and payable on demand. Borrower irrevocably appoints Lender as its attorney-in-fact, coupled with an interest, to take any action and execute any instrument reasonably necessary to exercise the rights granted in this Section, including applying for and obtaining Permits and BAR approvals in Borrower's name.
@H2:10.12|Suspension; Stop-Work.|Lender may direct Borrower to suspend the Renovation Work or any portion thereof if Lender reasonably determines that continued work would violate Applicable Law, would create a risk to health or safety, would violate the LUR or any environmental requirement, or would result in construction not in accordance with the Plans. Borrower shall comply with any such direction promptly and shall not resume work until Lender consents in writing. Any such suspension directed by Lender (other than a suspension resulting from Borrower's default) shall extend the Substantial Completion Deadline on a day-for-day basis.
@H2:10.13|No Obligation to Advance After Default.|Lender shall have no obligation to make any Advance from the Renovation Holdback, and may suspend all Advances, upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, upon the failure of any condition set forth in Section 10.5, or upon the occurrence of any event that, with notice or lapse of time or both, would constitute an Event of Default. Any failure by Lender to make an Advance under such circumstances shall not constitute a default by Lender or a breach of any obligation owed to Borrower, the General Contractor, or any other Person.
@H2:10.14|Mechanics' Liens and Notices of Nonresponsibility.|Borrower shall comply with Section 6.15. Borrower acknowledges that the Renovation Work and any tenant improvement work may give rise to mechanic's lien claims and that Lender's first-lien priority is dependent upon the timely recording of this Mortgage, the delivery of lien waivers, and the obtaining of the title date-down endorsements required hereby.
@H2:10.15|Construction Insurance.|Throughout the period from closing through Substantial Completion, Borrower shall maintain builder's risk insurance in accordance with Section 12.4 and shall cause the General Contractor and each subcontractor to maintain the insurance required by the Construction Contract, naming Lender as an additional insured and, with respect to builder's risk, as mortgagee and loss payee.
@H2:10.16|Close-Out Documents.|Within sixty (60) days after Substantial Completion, Borrower shall deliver to Lender (a) as-built drawings and specifications, (b) all warranties, guaranties, and operating manuals for the renovated systems, including the HVAC equipment and the elevator, (c) final unconditional lien waivers and a final contractor's affidavit, (d) a final title date-down endorsement and a final as-built survey if required by Lender, (e) evidence of the certificate of occupancy, and (f) a final cost certification and reconciliation of the Renovation Budget prepared by Borrower and certified by its chief financial officer or, if none, by the Key Principal.
@H2:10.17|Force Majeure.|"**Force Majeure**" means any delay caused by acts of God, fire, flood, hurricane, earthquake, war, terrorism, civil disturbance, epidemic, unusually severe weather, governmental order or moratorium (other than one caused by Borrower's violation of Applicable Law), or labor dispute not caused by Borrower, provided that (a) Borrower gives Lender written notice within ten (10) days after the commencement of the delay, (b) the delay is not caused by Borrower's failure to perform its obligations, including the timely payment of the General Contractor, and (c) Borrower diligently pursues completion. In no event shall Force Majeure relieve Borrower of the obligation to achieve Substantial Completion by June 15, 2026, except to the extent of a delay approved in writing by Lender, not to exceed sixty (60) days in the aggregate.

@H1:ARTICLE 11 — RESERVE AND ESCROW ACCOUNTS
@H2:11.1|Tax and Insurance Escrow.|Borrower shall deposit with Lender, on each Payment Date, an amount equal to one-twelfth (1/12) of the estimated annual real property taxes and casualty and liability insurance premiums for the Property, covering all three tax parcels (Charleston County Tax Map Nos. 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009) (the "**Tax and Insurance Escrow**"). Lender shall hold such deposits and apply them toward the payment of real property taxes and insurance premiums as they become due and payable. Lender may adjust the monthly escrow amount periodically based on actual or anticipated tax assessments and insurance premiums, and Borrower shall pay any deficiency within thirty (30) days after written demand. If a Tax and Insurance Escrow is not established or is waived by Lender in writing, Borrower shall nevertheless pay all Impositions before delinquency and deliver evidence of payment to Lender.
@H2:11.2|Capital Replacement Reserve.|Borrower shall deposit with Lender, on each Payment Date, the sum of Six Hundred Forty-Five Dollars and Eighty-Three Cents ($645.83) into a capital replacement reserve account (the "**Capital Replacement Reserve**"), being $0.25 per square foot per year multiplied by 31,000 square feet of gross building area ($7,750.00 per year), divided by twelve. Funds in the Capital Replacement Reserve shall be disbursed to Borrower upon Lender's approval of qualifying capital expenditures, subject to Lender's reasonable review and approval procedures, and shall be applied solely to capital repairs and replacements at the Property.
@H2:11.3|Tenant Improvement and Leasing Commission Reserve.|Borrower shall deposit at closing the sum of One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars ($150,000.00) into a tenant improvement and leasing commission reserve account (the "**TI/LC Reserve**") held by Lender. Disbursements from the TI/LC Reserve shall be subject to Lender's prior written approval and shall be used exclusively for tenant improvement costs and leasing commissions incurred in connection with the leasing of vacant space at the Property. Upon any draw from the TI/LC Reserve, Borrower shall replenish the TI/LC Reserve to the full amount of $150,000.00 from Borrower's own funds within thirty (30) days after Lender's written demand. Borrower acknowledges that the TI/LC Reserve is in addition to, and not in lieu of, the tenant improvement allowance line item of the Renovation Budget, and that leasing commissions are not otherwise funded by the Renovation Budget.
@H2:11.4|Reserve Accounts Generally.|Each Reserve Account shall be maintained by Lender in the name of Lender or its designee. The Reserve Accounts shall not bear interest unless required by Applicable Law, and any interest earned shall be held as part of the applicable Reserve Account. All sums in the Reserve Accounts shall constitute additional security for the Debt, and Borrower hereby grants to Lender a security interest in all Reserve Accounts and all sums held therein, including all proceeds thereof. The Reserve Accounts are not trust funds and Lender shall have no obligation to any creditor of Borrower with respect thereto. Lender may, at its option, apply any sums in the Reserve Accounts to the Debt upon an Event of Default or to cure any default by Borrower. Borrower shall have no right to require Lender to release or apply any sums except as expressly provided in this Article 11.
@H2:11.5|Failure to Deposit.|Borrower's failure to make any deposit required by this Article 11 within five (5) days after its due date shall constitute an Event of Default. Lender may, at its option, advance the amount of any required deposit on Borrower's behalf, and such advance shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10 bearing interest at the Default Rate.

@H1:ARTICLE 12 — INSURANCE
@H2:12.1|Property Insurance.|Borrower shall maintain at all times comprehensive all-risk (special form) property insurance covering the Property and all Improvements, on a replacement cost basis, with an agreed amount endorsement (waiver of coinsurance) and, if available, an ordinance or law endorsement. Such insurance shall be in an amount not less than the greater of the outstanding principal balance of the Loan or the full replacement cost of the Improvements, and shall name Lender as mortgagee and loss payee pursuant to a standard mortgagee clause. Coverage shall include, without limitation, fire, windstorm, hail, explosion, vandalism, malicious mischief, sprinkler leakage, water damage, and such other perils as Lender may reasonably require.
@H2:12.2|Commercial General Liability.|Borrower shall maintain commercial general liability insurance with minimum coverage limits of $2,000,000.00 per occurrence and $5,000,000.00 in the aggregate, naming Lender as an additional insured. Such insurance shall include coverage for premises liability, operations liability, products and completed operations, personal and advertising injury, and, during the Renovation Work, construction-related exposures.
@H2:12.3|Flood Insurance.|Borrower shall maintain flood insurance on the Property in an amount not less than $5,000,000.00, naming Lender as mortgagee and loss payee. Borrower acknowledges that the Property is understood to be located in FEMA Flood Zone X and that federally mandated flood insurance may not be required for property in Zone X, and that Lender nevertheless requires flood insurance coverage as a condition of the Loan. Borrower shall deliver to Lender, prior to closing and annually thereafter, a flood zone determination for the Property from a source acceptable to Lender. If the Property is determined to be located in a Special Flood Hazard Area, Borrower shall obtain and maintain flood insurance in the amount required by the Flood Disaster Protection Act and the regulations thereunder, and shall comply with all applicable requirements of Applicable Law relating to flood insurance.
@H2:12.4|Builder's Risk Insurance.|During the period from closing through Substantial Completion of the Renovation Work, Borrower shall maintain builder's risk insurance (on a completed value or course-of-construction basis) in an amount not less than the full Renovation Budget of $3,150,000.00, covering the Property and the Renovation Work against all risks of physical loss or damage during construction, and naming Lender as mortgagee and loss payee. Such coverage shall include soft costs, expediting expense, and, if applicable, coverage for the increased cost of construction due to changes in building codes.
@H2:12.5|Workers' Compensation; Umbrella or Excess Liability.|Borrower shall maintain (a) workers' compensation insurance in the amounts required by the laws of the State of South Carolina, covering all employees of Borrower and, to the extent not covered under the General Contractor's policies, all persons engaged in the Renovation Work; and (b) umbrella or excess liability insurance in an amount not less than $5,000,000.00, providing excess coverage over the commercial general liability, automobile liability, and employers' liability policies.
@H2:12.6|Carrier Requirements; Notice of Cancellation.|All insurance required under this Article 12 shall be issued by insurers licensed to do business in the State of South Carolina and having an A.M. Best rating of not less than A-:VII. Each policy shall contain a provision requiring not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender of cancellation, non-renewal, or material modification (ten (10) days' notice in the case of non-payment of premium). Each policy shall waive subrogation against Lender to the extent permitted by the policy and Applicable Law.
@H2:12.7|Evidence of Insurance; Renewals.|Prior to closing and thereafter not less than thirty (30) days prior to the expiration of each policy, Borrower shall deliver to Lender certificates of insurance and, upon request, certified copies of each policy, evidence of payment of premiums, and such other evidence as Lender may reasonably require. Borrower acknowledges that the certificates of insurance omit policy terms and conditions and that Lender's obligation to accept a certificate of insurance does not limit Lender's right to require delivery of the underlying policies or endorsements.
@H2:12.8|Application of Insurance Proceeds.|Borrower shall promptly notify Lender of any loss or damage to the Property. Lender shall be entitled to receive and hold all insurance proceeds (the "**Insurance Proceeds**"). Lender may, at its option, either (a) apply the Insurance Proceeds to the restoration of the Property, provided that (i) no Event of Default exists, (ii) in Lender's reasonable judgment the Property can be restored to its pre-loss condition with the available Insurance Proceeds, (iii) Borrower demonstrates to Lender's reasonable satisfaction its ability to fund any deficiency, and (iv) the restoration will be completed within a reasonable period; or (b) apply the Insurance Proceeds to the repayment of the Debt in accordance with Section 3.11, without payment of any prepayment premium, penalty, or Yield Maintenance Premium. Borrower hereby assigns to Lender all Insurance Proceeds and authorizes Lender to endorse any draft or instrument for such proceeds. Borrower shall pay any deductible.
@H2:12.9|Failure to Insure.|If Borrower fails to obtain or maintain any insurance required by this Article 12, Lender may, but shall not be obligated to, obtain such insurance and pay the premiums therefor, and all sums so paid, together with interest at the Default Rate, shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10. Borrower's failure to maintain any insurance required by this Article 12 shall constitute an Event of Default, without cure period, as provided in Section 15.3(c).

@H1:ARTICLE 13 — CONDEMNATION
@H2:13.1|Notice; Lender's Participation.|Borrower shall promptly notify Lender of any actual or threatened condemnation, eminent domain proceeding, or taking of all or any portion of the Property (a "**Taking**"), and shall deliver copies of all pleadings, notices, and correspondence relating thereto. Lender shall be entitled, at its option, to participate in any such proceeding at Borrower's expense.
@H2:13.2|Assignment of Award.|Borrower hereby absolutely assigns, transfers, and sets over to Lender all awards, compensation, damages, and other sums (the "**Condemnation Awards**") payable by reason of any Taking, including any award for the value of the Land taken, damages to the remainder, and interest thereon. Borrower authorizes Lender to collect and receive such Condemnation Awards directly, and Borrower irrevocably appoints Lender as its attorney-in-fact, coupled with an interest, to endorse any draft or instrument for such Condemnation Awards.
@H2:13.3|Application of Awards.|Lender may, at its option, either (a) apply the Condemnation Awards to the restoration of the Property on terms and conditions reasonably satisfactory to Lender, or (b) apply the Condemnation Awards to the repayment of the Debt in accordance with Section 3.11, without payment of any prepayment premium, penalty, or Yield Maintenance Premium. Borrower shall pay all costs and expenses of Lender incurred in connection with any Taking. If a Taking of any portion of the Property that provides access to the Property occurs, or if the Taking would materially impair the use or value of the Property, Lender may declare the Debt immediately due and payable, and any resulting prepayment shall be treated in accordance with Section 3.11.

@H1:ARTICLE 14 — FINANCIAL COVENANTS AND REPORTING
@H2:14.1|Debt Service Coverage Ratio.|Borrower shall maintain a minimum Debt Service Coverage Ratio ("**DSCR**") of not less than 1.25x, determined as follows:
@I:(a) "**Net Operating Income**" means, for the applicable period, the gross revenues of the Property from all sources, including Rents, expense reimbursements, and other income, determined on a trailing twelve (12) month basis in accordance with GAAP consistently applied, less (i) a vacancy and collection loss allowance equal to the greater of actual vacancy or five percent (5%) of gross potential rent, and (ii) operating expenses of the Property actually paid or payable, including real property taxes, insurance premiums, utilities, repairs and maintenance, management fees not exceeding four percent (4%) of gross revenues, and a replacement reserve of $0.25 per square foot per year, but excluding (A) depreciation, amortization, and other non-cash items, (B) interest expense and debt service, (C) income taxes, (D) capital expenditures, (E) any extraordinary or non-recurring items, and (F) any expense that is not attributable to the operation of the Property.
@I:(b) "**Annual Debt Service**" means the greater of (i) the aggregate amount of interest and principal that would be payable over the succeeding twelve (12) months under the Loan Documents based on the outstanding principal balance and the Note Rate as of the last day of the applicable period and the then-applicable amortization schedule, and (ii) the amount that would be payable over such twelve (12) month period if the outstanding principal balance were fully amortized over a twenty-five (25) year amortization schedule at the Note Rate. If the Loan is in the Interest-Only Period as of the last day of the applicable period, Annual Debt Service shall be calculated on a fully amortizing basis in accordance with clause (ii) of the preceding sentence.
@I:(c) DSCR shall be tested quarterly, commencing with the fiscal quarter ending June 30, 2027 (being the first full calendar quarter ending after the date that is twenty-four (24) months after the Closing Date), and continuing on the last day of each calendar quarter thereafter. Borrower shall deliver the compliance certificate required by Section 14.4 within thirty (30) days after the end of each such quarter.
@I:(d) A failure to maintain the required DSCR for any two (2) consecutive calendar quarters shall constitute an Event of Default, subject to the cure period provided in Section 15.3(b).
@H2:14.2|Net Worth and Liquidity.|Borrower shall maintain at all times during the term of the Loan (a) a net worth of not less than $1,000,000.00, and (b) liquid assets (defined as cash, cash equivalents, marketable securities, and unencumbered deposits held at federally insured depository institutions) of not less than $500,000.00. Compliance with this Section 14.2 shall be tested annually, based upon the financial statements and certifications delivered pursuant to Section 14.3. Guarantor's net worth is acknowledged to be approximately $28,000,000.00 as of the Closing Date; Guarantor has separately covenanted in the Guaranty to the financial covenants set forth therein, and the covenants in this Section 14.2 are in addition to, and not in limitation of, the covenants of Guarantor in the Guaranty.
@H2:14.3|Reporting Requirements.|Borrower shall deliver to Lender:
@I:(a) annual audited financial statements of Borrower, prepared in accordance with GAAP by an independent certified public accounting firm acceptable to Lender, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of Borrower's fiscal year, together with an unqualified opinion and, if required by Lender, a schedule of the computation of DSCR, net worth, and liquidity;
@I:(b) an annual personal financial statement of Guarantor, in form and detail satisfactory to Lender, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of each calendar year;
@I:(c) quarterly rent rolls for the Property, certified by Borrower as true, correct, and complete, within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter, identifying each Tenant, premises, lease expiration, base rent, escalation, security deposit, and any delinquency, and reconciling the in-place rents to the Rent Roll delivered at closing;
@I:(d) annual property operating statements for the Property, including a detailed income and expense report and comparison to budget, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of Borrower's fiscal year;
@I:(e) copies of all Leases and Lease modifications, and all estoppel certificates and SNDAs received from Tenants, within ten (10) Business Days after execution or receipt;
@I:(f) during the Renovation Work, monthly reports on the status of the Renovation Work, including percentage completion, cost-to-complete, change orders, and identification of any delay or budget variance;
@I:(g) the annual vapor barrier inspection report required by Section 9.3(c), within thirty (30) days after completion of the inspection;
@I:(h) copies of all SCDHEC correspondence and reports as required by Section 6.13 and Section 9.3(f);
@I:(i) promptly upon Lender's request, such other financial information and operating information as Lender may reasonably require; and
@I:(j) a compliance certificate in the form reasonably required by Lender, executed by a manager of Borrower (acting through the Key Principal), certifying compliance with Sections 14.1 and 14.2 and stating whether any Event of Default exists.
@H2:14.4|Compliance Certificate.|Each compliance certificate delivered under Section 14.3(j) shall set forth in reasonable detail the computations used in determining DSCR, net worth, and liquidity, and shall be certified as true and correct by the individual executing it. Lender may require supporting documentation for any computation.
@H2:14.5|Appraisals and Environmental Updates.|Lender may obtain, at Borrower's expense not more than once in any twelve (12) month period (and at any time following an Event of Default), an updated appraisal or appraisal review of the Property and an updated environmental assessment, and Borrower shall cooperate fully with the preparation thereof and pay the reasonable cost. Borrower acknowledges that Lender, as a state-chartered bank insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, is subject to the appraisal requirements of FIRREA and its implementing regulations and may be required to obtain and independently review appraisals in connection with the Loan.
@H2:14.6|Failure to Report.|Borrower's failure to deliver any report or certificate required by this Article 14 within the time specified, and the continuance of such failure for ten (10) days after written notice from Lender, shall constitute an Event of Default subject to the cure period in Section 15.3(b).
