@H1:ARTICLE 15 — EVENTS OF DEFAULT
@H2:15.1|Events of Default.|Each of the following shall constitute an Event of Default under this Mortgage:
@I:(a) **Payment.** Borrower fails to pay any installment of principal, interest, or any other amount due under the Loan Documents on the date when due, subject to the cure period set forth in Section 15.3(a);
@I:(b) **Covenant Default.** Borrower fails to observe, perform, or comply with any covenant, agreement, condition, or obligation contained in this Mortgage or any other Loan Document, and such failure continues beyond the applicable cure period set forth in Section 15.3(b); provided that any failure described in Section 15.3(c) shall constitute an immediate Event of Default without notice or cure;
@I:(c) **Representation Default.** Any representation or warranty made by Borrower or Guarantor in this Mortgage, in any other Loan Document, or in any certificate or report delivered to Lender proves to be materially false, misleading, or inaccurate in any material respect when made or deemed made;
@I:(d) **Insolvency.** Borrower or Guarantor files a petition in bankruptcy, or has filed against it an involuntary petition in bankruptcy that is not dismissed within sixty (60) days, or has a receiver, trustee, or custodian appointed for any substantial part of its property or assets, or makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors, or admits in writing its inability to pay its debts generally as they become due, or suffers any similar insolvency proceeding, or any member, manager, or Affiliate of Borrower files any such petition on behalf of Borrower without the consent required by Section 7.4;
@I:(e) **Cross-Default.** Borrower or Guarantor defaults under any other indebtedness for borrowed money in an amount exceeding $250,000.00, individually or in the aggregate, and such default is not cured within any applicable cure or grace period;
@I:(f) **Cross-Default Under Other Loan Documents.** An "Event of Default" occurs under the Note, the Guaranty, the Environmental Indemnity, or any other Loan Document (after giving effect to any applicable notice and cure period thereunder);
@I:(g) **Insurance.** Borrower fails to maintain any insurance required under Article 12 or any other Loan Document, or fails to deliver evidence of such insurance as required by Section 12.7;
@I:(h) **Transfer.** Borrower violates any of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 8.1 or any of the restrictions on subordinate or additional financing set forth in Section 8.2;
@I:(i) **Substantial Completion.** Borrower fails to achieve Substantial Completion of the Renovation Work on or before the Substantial Completion Deadline, as extended only in accordance with Section 10.3;
@I:(j) **DSCR.** Borrower fails to maintain the DSCR required by Section 14.1 for two (2) consecutive calendar quarters following the commencement of DSCR testing, subject to the cure period in Section 15.3(b);
@I:(k) **SPE Covenants.** Borrower breaches any of the single-purpose entity, separateness, Independent Manager, or bankruptcy-remoteness covenants set forth in Article 7;
@I:(l) **Environmental.** Borrower breaches any covenant set forth in Article 9, including any failure to comply with or any violation, modification, or termination of the LUR;
@I:(m) **Judgments; Attachments.** One or more judgments, orders, or decrees for the payment of money in an aggregate amount exceeding $250,000.00 (not covered by insurance as to which the insurer has acknowledged coverage in writing) is rendered against Borrower, Guarantor, or any Related Entity and remains unsatisfied, unvacated, unbonded, or unstayed on appeal for a period of thirty (30) consecutive days, or any writ of attachment, execution, or garnishment is issued against any portion of the Property or any Reserve Account;
@I:(n) **Material Adverse Change.** A material adverse change occurs in the financial condition, business, assets, or operations of Borrower, Guarantor, or any Related Entity that, in Lender's reasonable judgment, materially impairs the ability of Borrower to perform its obligations under the Loan Documents or of Guarantor to perform its obligations under the Guaranty;
@I:(o) **Sale or Encumbrance Without Consent.** The Property or any part thereof is sold, encumbered, or otherwise transferred, voluntarily or involuntarily, without Lender's prior written consent, including by operation of law, judicial sale, or transfer in lieu of foreclosure;
@I:(p) **Dissolution; Change of Control.** Borrower or any Related Entity dissolves, liquidates, merges, consolidates, or terminates its existence, or a change of control of Borrower or of any Related Entity occurs, in either case without Lender's prior written consent;
@I:(q) **Abandonment.** Borrower abandons the Property or suspends the operation of the Property or the Renovation Work for more than twenty (20) consecutive days (other than as permitted by Section 6.9 or Section 10.17); and
@I:(r) **Other.** Any other event or condition occurs that constitutes an Event of Default under any other Loan Document, or that constitutes a default under Applicable Law entitling Lender to accelerate the Debt or foreclose this Mortgage.
@H2:15.2|Notice of Default.|Lender may, but shall not be obligated to, deliver to Borrower written notice of any default or Event of Default. Except where this Mortgage expressly provides that no notice or cure period applies, the delivery of such notice shall not be a condition to the exercise of Lender's remedies, except that the cure periods set forth in Section 15.3 shall run from the date of such notice where this Mortgage so provides.
@H2:15.3|Cure Periods.|The following cure periods shall apply to the Events of Default described in Section 15.1:
@I:(a) **Payment Defaults.** Five (5) Business Days from the date on which payment was due. Lender shall not be obligated to accept any late payment, and acceptance of a late payment shall not constitute a waiver of any Event of Default arising from such late payment.
@I:(b) **Non-Monetary Defaults.** Thirty (30) calendar days after written notice from Lender to Borrower of such default; provided, however, that if the default is of a nature that it cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) calendar days, and Borrower has commenced and is diligently pursuing the cure thereof, the cure period shall be extended for an additional period not to exceed sixty (60) calendar days (for a total cure period not to exceed ninety (90) calendar days). The cure period in this Section 15.3(b) shall not apply to (i) any default described in Section 15.3(c), (ii) any default that cannot be cured as a practical matter, including any default arising from a transfer in violation of Section 8.1 or from the failure to achieve Substantial Completion by the Substantial Completion Deadline, or (iii) any default arising from the failure to pay money.
@I:(c) **Defaults Without Cure.** No notice or cure period shall apply to (i) any breach of the SPE covenants set forth in Article 7, (ii) any breach of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 8.1, (iii) any breach of the restrictions on subordinate or additional financing set forth in Section 8.2, (iv) any failure to maintain insurance required by Article 12, (v) any breach of Article 9 described in the final sentence of Section 9.7, (vi) any Event of Default described in Section 15.1(a) occurring after the second late payment in any twelve (12) month period, or (vii) any voluntary bankruptcy filing or other event described in Section 15.1(d) involving a voluntary act of Borrower. Each such breach shall constitute an immediate Event of Default, and Lender may exercise all remedies immediately and without notice.

@H1:ARTICLE 16 — REMEDIES
@H2:16.1|Acceleration.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may, at its option, declare the entire unpaid principal balance of the Debt, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and all other amounts due, to be immediately due and payable, without notice, presentment, protest, demand, or any other action, all of which are hereby expressly waived. Upon any Event of Default described in Section 15.1(d), the entire Debt shall automatically become immediately due and payable without any declaration or other act by Lender. The Debt shall also bear interest at the Default Rate as provided in Section 3.4.
@H2:16.2|Judicial Foreclosure; No Power of Sale.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may foreclose this Mortgage by an action in foreclosure filed in the Court of Common Pleas for Charleston County, South Carolina, or in any other court of competent jurisdiction, and may pursue all other remedies available at law or in equity. Borrower acknowledges that the State of South Carolina is a judicial foreclosure jurisdiction and that Lender has no power of sale. Nothing in this Mortgage authorizes Lender to sell the Property without judicial process, and any provision of this Mortgage that might be construed to confer such a power is hereby expressly disclaimed and shall be of no force or effect. Lender may, at its option, proceed to foreclose this Mortgage, to enforce the Note, or to pursue its other remedies, in any order or simultaneously, and may maintain successive actions.
@H2:16.3|Receiver.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default (and, in the case of a default consisting of a violation of Section 8.1 or Section 15.1(d), without regard to whether the Property is adequate security), Lender shall be entitled, as a matter of right and without notice, to the appointment of a receiver of the Property and of the Rents, and Borrower consents to such appointment and waives any objection thereto, including any objection based upon the adequacy of the security or the existence of a remedy at law. Borrower shall not oppose any application for the appointment of a receiver, and the appointment of a receiver shall not constitute an election of remedies or preclude foreclosure.
@H2:16.4|Entry and Possession; Mortgagee in Possession.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may enter upon and take possession of the Property and may operate, manage, and lease the Property, collect the Rents, make repairs, and pay operating expenses. Lender shall not be liable for any loss resulting from such action except to the extent caused by Lender's gross negligence or willful misconduct, and Lender may resign as mortgagee in possession at any time. Borrower shall surrender possession of the Property to Lender upon demand.
@H2:16.5|UCC Remedies.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may exercise all rights and remedies of a secured party under the UCC, including without limitation the right to take possession of the Personal Property, to require Borrower to assemble the Personal Property and make it available at a place designated by Lender, and to sell, lease, license, or otherwise dispose of the Personal Property at public or private sale. Lender shall give Borrower not less than ten (10) days' prior written notice of any disposition of the Personal Property (which the parties agree is commercially reasonable), and may purchase at any such sale. Lender may conduct any such sale separately from any foreclosure of the Land and Improvements, and the exercise of any UCC remedy shall not affect the lien of this Mortgage on the Land and Improvements.
@H2:16.6|Enforcement of Assignment of Rents.|Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may enforce the assignment of Leases and Rents in accordance with Article 4, may collect the Rents directly, and may apply the Rents as provided in Section 3.6. Lender's exercise of this remedy shall not constitute an election of remedies and shall not affect its right to foreclose this Mortgage.
@H2:16.7|Application of Proceeds.|The proceeds of any foreclosure sale, any sale under the UCC, and any other amounts received by Lender upon enforcement of the Loan Documents shall be applied in the following order: first, to the costs and expenses of enforcement, including reasonable attorneys' fees, court costs, and receiver's fees; second, to protective advances and any other sums advanced by Lender; third, to accrued and unpaid interest (including interest at the Default Rate); fourth, to the outstanding principal balance; fifth, to any other amounts due under the Loan Documents; and sixth, the remainder, if any, to the Persons entitled thereto under Applicable Law.
@H2:16.8|Deficiency.|If the proceeds of any sale or other disposition of the Property are insufficient to pay the Debt in full, Borrower and any other Person liable for the Debt shall remain liable for the deficiency to the extent permitted by Applicable Law, and Lender may seek a deficiency judgment in accordance with Applicable Law. Borrower acknowledges that South Carolina law may limit or condition the availability of a deficiency judgment and that nothing herein shall be construed to expand Lender's rights beyond those permitted by Applicable Law.
@H2:16.9|Cumulative Remedies; No Waiver; No Election.|No remedy conferred upon Lender is intended to be exclusive of any other remedy. Each remedy is cumulative and in addition to every other remedy available at law or in equity. No delay or omission by Lender in exercising any right or remedy shall impair such right or remedy or constitute a waiver thereof. Any single or partial exercise of any right or remedy shall not preclude any other or further exercise thereof. Lender may exercise any remedy without prejudice to any other remedy, and the exercise of one remedy shall not constitute an election of remedies.
@H2:16.10|Protective Advances; Lender's Right to Cure.|If Borrower fails to perform any obligation under this Mortgage, or if Lender reasonably determines that it is necessary to protect its interest in the Property, Lender may (but shall not be obligated to) make any payment, perform any obligation, or take any other action, including paying taxes, insurance premiums, Impositions, mechanic's liens, or judgment liens, performing any repair or maintenance, satisfying any environmental obligation, or completing the Renovation Work. All sums so advanced shall be a "**protective advance**," shall bear interest at the Default Rate from the date advanced until repaid, shall be secured by this Mortgage, and shall be immediately due and payable on demand. No such advance shall constitute a waiver of any Event of Default or an agreement to make any further advance.
@H2:16.11|Costs and Attorneys' Fees.|Borrower shall pay on demand all costs and expenses, including reasonable attorneys' fees, court costs, expert witness fees, title costs, and receiver's fees, incurred by Lender in connection with (a) the administration of the Loan following an Event of Default, (b) the enforcement or preservation of any right or remedy under the Loan Documents, including any foreclosure, bankruptcy, or appellate proceeding, (c) any workout, forbearance, or modification of the Loan, and (d) any dispute relating to the Property. Such amounts shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10.
@H2:16.12|Power of Attorney.|Borrower hereby irrevocably appoints Lender as its attorney-in-fact, coupled with an interest, with full power of substitution, to take any action and execute, acknowledge, and deliver any instrument that Lender deems necessary or desirable to (a) record this Mortgage or any amendment, (b) file or continue any UCC financing statement or fixture filing, (c) deliver a Rent Notice or enforce the assignment of Leases and Rents, (d) complete the Renovation Work and obtain Permits and BAR approvals, (e) pay taxes, insurance premiums, or liens, and (f) take any other action permitted under Section 16.10. This power of attorney is coupled with an interest and is irrevocable until the Debt is paid in full.
@H2:16.13|Waivers.|To the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Law, Borrower waives (a) any right to require Lender to marshal assets or to proceed against any particular Person or security, (b) any right to require Lender to pursue any other remedy before proceeding against the Property, (c) all rights of homestead, exemption, and appraisement, (d) all rights of redemption, reinstatement, or reinstatement of this Mortgage after a foreclosure sale, except any right that cannot lawfully be waived, (e) the benefit of any statute of limitations, stay, valuation, or appraisal, and (f) presentment, demand, protest, notice of intent to accelerate, notice of acceleration, and notice of nonpayment. Borrower acknowledges that South Carolina law may provide statutory rights of redemption and statutory upset-bid procedures in connection with a judicial foreclosure sale, that such rights are not waivable by agreement, and that nothing in this Section shall be construed as an attempt to waive any right that Applicable Law does not permit to be waived.
@H2:16.14|Lender as Mortgagee in Possession; Environmental.|If Lender enters upon or takes possession of the Property, Lender shall not, by reason of such entry or possession, be deemed to have assumed any liability for environmental conditions at the Property that existed prior to such entry, and Lender may take such actions as it deems appropriate to preserve the value of the Property and to comply with Environmental Laws.
@H2:16.15|Effect of Foreclosure on Guaranties.|No foreclosure, sale, or other enforcement action shall affect the liability of Guarantor under the Guaranty or of Borrower or Guarantor under the Environmental Indemnity, and Lender may proceed against Guarantor or under the Environmental Indemnity without first foreclosing this Mortgage.
TXTEOF
