@H2:16.11|Costs and Attorneys' Fees.|Borrower shall pay on demand all costs and expenses, including reasonable attorneys' fees, court costs, expert witness fees, title costs, and receiver's fees, incurred by Lender in connection with (a) the administration of the Loan following an Event of Default, (b) the enforcement or preservation of any right or remedy under the Loan Documents, including any foreclosure, bankruptcy, or appellate proceeding, (c) any workout, forbearance, or modification of the Loan, and (d) any dispute relating to the Property. Such amounts shall be a protective advance under Section 16.10.
@H2:16.12|Power of Attorney.|Borrower hereby irrevocably appoints Lender as its attorney-in-fact, coupled with an interest, with full power of substitution, to take any action and execute, acknowledge, and deliver any instrument that Lender deems necessary or desirable to (a) record this Mortgage or any amendment, (b) file or continue any UCC financing statement or fixture filing, (c) deliver a Rent Notice or enforce the assignment of Leases and Rents, (d) complete the Renovation Work and obtain Permits and BAR approvals, (e) pay taxes, insurance premiums, or liens, and (f) take any other action permitted under Section 16.10. This power of attorney is coupled with an interest and is irrevocable until the Debt is paid in full.
@H2:16.13|Waivers.|To the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Law, Borrower waives (a) any right to require Lender to marshal assets or to proceed against any particular Person or security, (b) any right to require Lender to pursue any other remedy before proceeding against the Property, (c) all rights of homestead, exemption, and appraisement, (d) all rights of redemption, reinstatement, or reinstatement of this Mortgage after a foreclosure sale, except any right that cannot lawfully be waived, (e) the benefit of any statute of limitations, stay, valuation, or appraisal, and (f) presentment, demand, protest, notice of intent to accelerate, notice of acceleration, and notice of nonpayment. Borrower acknowledges that South Carolina law may provide statutory rights of redemption and statutory upset-bid procedures in connection with a judicial foreclosure sale, that such rights are not waivable by agreement, and that nothing in this Section shall be construed as an attempt to waive any right that Applicable Law does not permit to be waived.
@H2:16.14|Lender as Mortgagee in Possession; Environmental.|If Lender enters upon or takes possession of the Property, Lender shall not, by reason of such entry or possession, be deemed to have assumed any liability for environmental conditions at the Property that existed prior to such entry, and Lender may take such actions as it deems appropriate to preserve the value of the Property and to comply with Environmental Laws.
@H2:16.15|Effect of Foreclosure on Guaranties.|No foreclosure, sale, or other enforcement action shall affect the liability of Guarantor under the Guaranty or of Borrower or Guarantor under the Environmental Indemnity, and Lender may proceed against Guarantor or under the Environmental Indemnity without first foreclosing this Mortgage.
