@H1:ARTICLE 17 — EXCULPATION AND RECOURSE
@H2:17.1|Limited Recourse.|Except as otherwise provided in this Article 17, the Environmental Indemnity, and the Guaranty, Lender's sole recourse for the payment and performance of the Debt shall be against the Property and the other collateral described in Article 2, and no judgment for any deficiency upon the Debt shall be sought or obtained by Lender against Borrower. Borrower shall not be personally liable for the payment of the principal of, or interest on, the Note or for any other amount due under the Loan Documents, except as provided in this Article 17.
@H2:17.2|Full Recourse Carve-Outs.|Notwithstanding Section 17.1, Borrower shall be fully and personally liable for the entire Debt (and not merely for the losses described in Section 17.3) if any of the following occurs:
@I:(a) fraud, intentional misrepresentation, or willful misconduct by Borrower, Guarantor, any Related Entity, or any of their respective agents or affiliates in connection with the Loan or any Loan Document;
@I:(b) the misapplication or misappropriation of any Rents (including security deposits), Insurance Proceeds, Condemnation Awards, or Escrow Funds or other Reserve Account funds, or the failure to apply any such amounts in accordance with the Loan Documents;
@I:(c) the voluntary commencement by or on behalf of Borrower of any case or proceeding under the United States Bankruptcy Code or any other federal or state insolvency, receivership, or similar law, or the voluntary consent to or acquiescence in any such filing or the appointment of a receiver, trustee, or custodian, in each case without the consent required by Section 7.4;
@I:(d) any transfer, encumbrance, or other transaction in violation of Section 8.1 or Section 8.2, including any transfer of a direct or indirect interest in Borrower effected without Lender's consent;
@I:(e) any breach of the SPE, separateness, Independent Manager, or bankruptcy-remoteness covenants set forth in Article 7; and
@I:(f) the failure to maintain insurance as required by Article 12 if such failure results in uninsured loss or damage to the Property.
@H2:17.3|Losses-Only Recourse|In addition to the full recourse events described in Section 17.2, Borrower shall be personally liable, but only to the extent of the actual losses, costs, damages, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) incurred by Lender, for (a) any physical waste of the Property committed by Borrower or any Person under its control; (b) any breach of Article 9 or of any Environmental Law, without duplication of amounts recoverable under the Environmental Indemnity; (c) any failure to pay real property taxes or insurance premiums to the extent Lender has not advanced funds for such purpose or to the extent of any escrow shortfall; (d) any Rents, security deposits, or other amounts collected by Borrower after an Event of Default and not delivered to Lender as required by Article 4; and (e) any fees, costs, or expenses paid to Borrower's Affiliates in violation of Section 6.18 or Section 8.7.
@H2:17.4|Environmental Indemnity; Full Recourse.|The obligations of Borrower and Guarantor under the Environmental Indemnity are full recourse obligations and are not limited by Section 17.1 or by the exculpation provisions of this Article 17. Lender may enforce the Environmental Indemnity directly against Borrower and Guarantor without first foreclosing this Mortgage or exhausting any other remedy.
@H2:17.5|Guaranty.|Guarantor's obligations under the Guaranty, including the non-recourse carve-out guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, and the payment guaranty for interest shortfall described in Section 5.5 of the Term Sheet, are independent of Borrower's obligations and shall not be limited or impaired by this Article 17. Lender may proceed against Guarantor at any time, without first foreclosing this Mortgage or exhausting its remedies against the Property.
@H2:17.6|No Impairment of Lien or Remedies.|Nothing in this Article 17 shall limit, impair, or impair the Liens, security interests, and assignment created by this Mortgage or any of Lender's remedies in Article 16. Lender may exercise all of its rights and remedies against the Property and the other collateral regardless of whether any of the events described in Section 17.2 or Section 17.3 has occurred.
@H2:17.7|Reinstatement.|If Lender is required to surrender or return any payment or proceeds received in connection with the Debt by reason of any bankruptcy, insolvency, or similar proceeding, the Debt shall be deemed to have continued in existence to the extent of such payment or proceeds, and this Article 17 shall continue in full force and effect.

@H1:ARTICLE 18 — MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS
@H2:18.1|Governing Law.|This Mortgage shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of South Carolina, without regard to principles of conflicts of law that would require the application of the laws of another jurisdiction.
@H2:18.2|Venue; Consent to Jurisdiction.|Borrower irrevocably submits to the jurisdiction of the courts of the State of South Carolina and the United States District Court for the District of South Carolina for the purpose of any suit, action, or proceeding arising out of or relating to this Mortgage or any other Loan Document, and waives any objection to venue in Charleston County, South Carolina. Nothing in this Section shall limit Lender's right to enforce any judgment in any jurisdiction.
@H2:18.3|Waiver of Jury Trial.|TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, BORROWER AND LENDER EACH HEREBY KNOWINGLY, VOLUNTARILY, AND INTENTIONALLY WAIVE ANY RIGHT TO A TRIAL BY JURY IN ANY ACTION OR PROCEEDING ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS MORTGAGE, ANY OTHER LOAN DOCUMENT, OR THE LOAN.
@H2:18.4|Notices.|All notices, demands, consents, and other communications under this Mortgage shall be in writing and shall be deemed given (a) when delivered personally, (b) one (1) Business Day after deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier, (c) three (3) Business Days after deposit in the United States mail, certified or registered, return receipt requested, postage prepaid, or (d) when sent by electronic mail, provided that an email notice of default or acceleration shall also be delivered by one of the methods described in clauses (a) through (c). Notices shall be addressed as follows, or to such other address as a party designates by written notice:
@TABLE:2.9,3.6
Borrower|Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, 88 Broad Street, Suite 200, Charleston, South Carolina 29401, Attention: Neil Ashford Graydon, with a copy to Cartwright & Lyons LLP, [address], Attention: [________]
Lender|Calverley Heritage Bank, 412 Whitaker Street, Savannah, Georgia 31401, Attention: Marcus Prideaux, Senior Vice President — Commercial Real Estate Lending, with a copy to Fielding, Ashworth & Cole LLP, 1201 King Street, Suite 300, Charleston, South Carolina 29403, Attention: Catherine Ashworth
@ENDTABLE
@H2:18.5|Successors and Assigns; No Assignment by Borrower.|This Mortgage shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of Borrower and Lender and their respective successors and permitted assigns. Lender may assign, sell participations in, or otherwise transfer the Loan and this Mortgage, in whole or in part, without Borrower's consent, and Borrower acknowledges that any such assignee shall be entitled to all of the rights of Lender hereunder. Borrower may not assign or transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Mortgage.
@H2:18.6|Severability.|If any provision of this Mortgage is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable in any respect, such provision shall be enforced to the maximum extent permitted by Applicable Law, and the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
@H2:18.7|Entire Agreement; Amendments.|The Loan Documents constitute the entire agreement between Borrower and Lender with respect to the Loan and supersede all prior agreements, understandings, and negotiations, whether written or oral, relating thereto, including the Term Sheet to the extent inconsistent herewith as provided in Section 1.6. This Mortgage may be amended only by a written instrument executed by Borrower and Lender.
@H2:18.8|No Partnership or Joint Venture.|Nothing in this Mortgage or any other Loan Document shall be construed to create a partnership, joint venture, or fiduciary relationship between Borrower and Lender. Lender is acting solely as a lender and secured party.
@H2:18.9|Indemnification.|Borrower shall indemnify, defend, and hold Lender harmless from and against any and all claims, actions, suits, liabilities, losses, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees and court costs) arising out of or relating to (a) the ownership, operation, leasing, renovation, or condition of the Property, (b) any act or omission of Borrower or any Person under its control, (c) any breach by Borrower of any Loan Document, and (d) any claim by any Member, Tenant, contractor, or other Person relating to the Property, the Loan, or the transactions contemplated hereby; provided that Borrower shall not be obligated to indemnify Lender for claims to the extent caused by Lender's gross negligence or willful misconduct.
@H2:18.10|Counterparts; Electronic Signatures.|This Mortgage may be executed in any number of counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, and all of which together shall constitute one instrument. Delivery of an executed counterpart by facsimile or electronic mail (including PDF) shall have the same effect as delivery of an originally executed counterpart. Borrower shall deliver such number of original counterparts as Lender requires for recording.
@H2:18.11|Recordation; Additional Amounts.|Borrower shall cause this Mortgage to be recorded in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, promptly following the Closing Date, and shall pay all recording fees and documentary stamp taxes. Borrower shall, upon Lender's request, execute and deliver an affidavit of the amount of the Debt outstanding, a certificate of no offset or defense, and any other instrument reasonably required for the enforcement or release of this Mortgage.
@H2:18.12|Usury; Savings.|The provisions of Section 3.12 are incorporated herein by this reference.
@H2:18.13|Joint and Several; Single-Member Entity.|Borrower acknowledges that it is the sole owner of the Property and that any reference in the Loan Documents to the obligations of Borrower being joint and several is inapplicable. Borrower shall not permit the admission of any additional member to Borrower without Lender's prior written consent in accordance with Section 8.1.
@H2:18.14|Waiver of Right to Assert Defenses.|Borrower waives, to the fullest extent permitted by Applicable Law, the right to assert against Lender any defense, counterclaim, or offset arising out of any act or omission of Borrower, any prior owner of the Property, or any third party.
@H2:18.15|Interpretation of Remedies.|In the event that any provision of this Mortgage granting Lender a remedy is determined unenforceable in whole or in part, such determination shall not affect the enforceability of any other remedy or provision.
@H2:18.16|Further Assurances.|Borrower shall, at its own cost, do all such further acts and things and execute, acknowledge, and deliver all such further documents, certificates, and instruments as Lender may reasonably require to give effect to the provisions of this Mortgage.
@H2:18.17|Satisfaction of Mortgage.|Upon payment in full of the Debt, Lender shall, at Borrower's expense, execute and deliver a satisfaction of this Mortgage in recordable form and appropriate UCC termination statements, as provided in Section 2.7.

