@H1:8. OPEN ITEMS AND INSTRUCTIONS REQUESTED
@P:The following decisions are required before the draft is released to Marcus on April 1. Items marked "closing-blocking" must be resolved before the Loan Documents are executed.
@L:**1. DSCR covenant (closing-blocking).** The 1.25x covenant cannot be satisfied at any projection in the record. Please direct one of: (a) re-size the Loan; (b) reduce the covenant level; (c) extend the interest-only period beyond month 24; (d) defer the first test date; (e) convert the covenant into a cash-management trigger with a DSCR cure deposit right, which is our recommendation for a value-add loan of this kind; or (f) leave the covenant as drafted with the consequences accepted and documented.
@L:**2. Appraisal (closing-blocking).** Confirm that Lender will obtain an independent appraisal review and require a corrected or supplemental report reconciling the income approach. Confirm that Borrower bears the cost under Term Sheet § 13.2(b).
@L:**3. Sources and uses (closing-blocking).** Confirm how the $150,000 TI/LC reserve, the $147,500 origination fee, the $54,575 recording tax, and third-party closing costs are to be funded, given that the initial advance plus non-renovation equity exactly equals the purchase price.
@L:**4. NOI and Annual Debt Service definitions.** Confirm whether Annual Debt Service is to be calculated on a fully amortizing basis during the interest-only period (as drafted, and as the Rent Roll assumes) or on the basis of actual payments then required.
@L:**5. Lease consent threshold.** Confirm whether to reduce the 5,000 square foot threshold, or add a specific consent right for Bay 2 and Bay 3, so that Lender controls the letting of the vacant ground-floor bays.
@L:**6. Net worth and liquidity obligor.** Confirm Borrower, Guarantor, or both.
@L:**7. Insurance default cure.** Confirm whether a five-business-day cure should be available for an inadvertent lapse in coverage and proof of reinstatement.
@L:**8. Yield maintenance.** Confirm the Term Sheet formulation (7.1 above).
@L:**9. Lockout remedy.** Confirm the approach in 7.2 above.
@L:**10. Casualty and condemnation at par.** Confirm the concession in 7.3 above.
@L:**11. DSCR test date.** Confirm June 30, 2027 (Term Sheet operative language) or April 15, 2027 (Rent Roll and your note).
@L:**12. Audited financial statements.** Confirm whether to require audited statements (Term Sheet § 7.3(a)) or reviewed statements with certification (Operating Agreement § 6.2(b)).
@L:**13. Force Majeure and the completion date.** Confirm whether the Substantial Completion Deadline should shift day-for-day if the closing is delayed, and whether the sixty-day Force Majeure cap is adequate given hurricane exposure.
@L:**14. Affiliate fees.** Confirm that subordination and suspension of GDG's asset management and development management fees (Mortgage § 6.18) is required, notwithstanding that the Term Sheet is silent.
@L:**15. Upstream transfers and change of control.** Confirm that the Section 8.1(c) extension to indirect transfers and changes of control is non-negotiable.
@L:**16. Instrument type.** Confirm that Lender wants a mortgage rather than a deed of trust (the Term Sheet specifies a mortgage; both are used in South Carolina and the remedies are the same).
@L:**17. Cash management.** Confirm whether Lender wants a lockbox or cash-management arrangement at closing or as a springing trigger on a DSCR shortfall. The Term Sheet is silent and the draft contains no cash management provisions.

@H1:9. RECOMMENDED ADDITIONS TO THE CLOSING CONDITIONS
@P:The following should be added to Term Sheet § 12.1 (or documented as conditions in the closing checklist) before the Loan Documents are executed. Items in italics are conditions precedent that Lender should not waive.
@L:**Operating Agreement Amendment**, executed by all three Members, adding the Independent Manager requirement, the separateness covenants, the single-purpose restriction, and the unanimity requirement for bankruptcy, dissolution, merger, and consolidation. *Do not waive.*
